{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20","id":1563478,"title":"Feedback on a homebrew Path of Enlightenment [V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-25T13:59:14-07:00","id":1563478,"title":"Feedback on a homebrew Path of Enlightenment [V20]","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm looking for some feedback on a homebrew Path of Enlightenment I'm working on.<br /> <br /> My motivation is to fill a gap in the existing Paths that I see for vampires who recognize that they are no longer human, but aim for co-existence as much as personal fulfillment. Paths with Instinct as a Virtue always have the problem that they create an incompatibility with societal structures, often emphasized by using Conviction as well.<br /> <br /> The few Paths with Conscience and Self-Control only cover a very narrow spectrum of characters. I wanted to try something that can be broader in application, or at least fill in between Path of Redemption and Honorable Accord. I'm looking for feedback on whether the Path would be interesting enough for a character, whether the concept and descriptions are clear enough to understand, and of course whether you could see it working or not.<br /> <br /> Just in case, but important: while the Path clearly borrows from Thelema, <i>it is not Thelema</i>, nor is it meant as a commentary on it. The core actually comes from the Via Voluptarius and Via Adversarius in DAV; I only noticed the Thelemic elements later and decided to go with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Path of Desire and True Will</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The origins of this Path can be traced back to the much older Road of Sin. There are key differences though: while it identifies desire as the driving force of both Beast and vampire, it tries to balance the ego-centrism of the Road by integrating it with society. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">It stipulates that while personal development in a vacuum may be possible, the benefits of a society to the individual are by far too useful to dismiss. Instead of restricting the follower of the Path to a specific social dogma, it relies on the understanding of how social integration will emerge from their True Will as a natural consequence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">True Will can be described as a purpose or path through life. It is refined through reflection on desires and shaped into a more holistic concept: True Will means mindfulness of the path as it progresses. Disruptive desires will inevitably create conflict, which by itself will hinder further progression \u2013 by getting what you want, you may find yourself barred from what you want. So is this truly what you want?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Path takes this idea of refinement of desire into True Will, and applies it to the nature of vampires: desires are the root that nurture the Will and stem from the vampire or the Beast, not from a divine mandate. Motivations will change over time, and evolution is an important part of traveling the Path. The single most important aspect for a follower is to be always conscious of whether the consequences of their actions will allow them to continue their journey; True Will is the goal as much as the path itself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Much greater emphasis is put on control of the Beast than was usual for the Road of Sin. The Beast is a part of the vampire they must find a common ground with, but set strict lines that cannot be crossed. There is no reason to deny the Beast pleasure in feeding, or indulgence in other desires \u2013 but there can be no quarter if the urges would imperil the Will of the vampire. This stick-and-carrot approach eschews compromise. Either a desire can be transformed or adapted to satisfy the Beast, or it is denied.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Path seeks to mediate realization of the Self (Courage) with the Beast (Self-Control) and society (Conscience). Therefore, a sin for each is given in the hierarchy; however, these are ultimately the same concept expressed through the three different lenses and should be understood as such.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Virtues:</b> Conscience, Self-Control</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ethics:</b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Act mindful. All your actions will be reflected back onto you. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Beast belongs to you, but you do not belong to it.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Share in your desires, but refuse unwanted ones. Do not compromise.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Freedom, control, and will are your most valuable tools. Do not lose them.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is no growth on toxic soil. Cultivate your environment as you would yourself.</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Hierarchy of Sins</b></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Path of Desire and True Will</span></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rating</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Moral Guideline</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rationale</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">10</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Feeling regret for willful action </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Feeling shame for willful action </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Feeling guilt for willful action</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If an action causes regret, shame, or guilt, it could not have been willful.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">9</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Acting without will </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Acting instinctively </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ignoring the reflection of your actions in others</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thoughtless action creates infertile soil for willful action. Be mindful of how your actions affect future progress.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">8</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Harming yourself, without will </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Refusing indulgence that harms none</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Harming others, without will</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Self-hate, starving your Beast, or creating a hostile environment can only inhibit your progress. They serve no purpose.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">7</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failing to explore a new desire</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ignoring the desires of your Beast</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Refusing to engage with society</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is no progress without expansion, nor in denial or isolation. Do not accept unwanted desires, but instead transform them.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">6</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failing to evolve your desires</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Letting your Beast taint your desires</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Associating with those who foul your desires</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stagnant and putrid will has lost its purpose, progress is preserverence and growth. Cut off sick limbs, cull poisenous desires.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failing to act on your will</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Denying your Beast to act when in accordance with your will</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Denying others their desires unless they harm yours</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Inaction means forfeiting progress. Not using the fuel for your desires others may provide is a waste.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Losing your force of will </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Refusing to will your Beast into submission when necessary</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Submitting your will to another</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Force empowers, control adjucates, freedom enables. If you lose either, you lose the very means to your progress.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Acting contrary to your will</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Allowing your Beast to act contrary to your will</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Adhering to laws that stifle your will</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Any authority that inhibits your will is void. If you find yourself agreeing with such a restriction, you have not found your true will.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failing to understand your desires and will</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mistaking instinct for desire</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mistaking conformity for will</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">To do what thou wilt, know what thou wilt. Understand from where a disire stems and where it leads before recognizing it as will.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Becoming devoid of desire</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Relying only on the base desires of your Beast</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Relying only on the desires of others</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You can not build upon what is not your own.</span></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T21:31:38-07:00","id":1563486,"title":"","content":"The problem I see is that it's hard to use in practice.<br /> <br /> A Hierarchy of Sins has to be clear and objective. Deciding if a sin occurred or not must be as unambiguous as possible, the best case being an objective behavior. That's the greatest challenge with Paths built around open ended goals like &quot;do what you will&quot;.<br /> <br /> Reading the list, I don't know how I'm supposed to judge a real case. Looking at each level, in a inverted order:<br /> 1. I can't know if the character want something for themselves. I can see if what they desire is the desire of the Beast of another, but not if no other motivation exist.<br /> 2. How can I say if a character understand their own desire of not? How can I distinguish the mistake between instinct/desire or conformity/will and legitimate overlap, especially in a Path that teaches precisely the need for indulgence of the Beast's desires and following of social norms?<br /> 3. How can I access the character's will to say when it's being stifled vs followed?<br /> 4. Those work well when the Path gives clear parameters for what you should seek, but when the point is one's own will I can't say if it was lost or not, if submitting the Beast is necessary or if appeasement of another is submission or desire.<br /> 5. Unless you define this one as any dice roll failure, the problem again is that all of those rely on knowing beforehand what the character will or desire. If I didn't act, who can say I willed otherwise? Who can say I didn't will my Beast to do what it did? If my desire is to harm those of others, then what?<br /> 6. Those are antithetical to your stipulations: I can't evolve my desires if I can't be tainted by the desires if others. I can't accept and indulge the Beast without letting it influence me. I can't associate with people without a risk of having my desires regularly fouled. This is nonsense.<br /> 7. Demand to expand, indulge and engage with society, without recognizing they clan clash. It's one thing for a Path to demand two conflicting goals for you to find a balance, it's another for it to be unaware of the conflict to begin with.<br /> 8. The description doesn't follow prescription. I can apply if I interpret it as &quot;harming anyone by accident&quot;, but the description indicates this is nota The intention. Again, it relies on knowing beforehand a will from the character that can be anything.<br /> 9. How can I say an action occurred without will? How do I measure self reflection?<br /> 10. This is the only bone close to be actionable and still requires to assess feelings that may be masked for any reason.<br /> <br /> Now, my impression of the whole project is that you're trying to fill a perceived gap without asking what the narrative goal of the Path is.<br /> <br /> This is basically an awkward Path of What I'd Do Anyway, and one that's literally that, it exists for the character to act freely, without ideology or pressure beyond wanting to do whatever you did. The reason this gap exists isn't negligence, but that Paths were made precisely to not do that.<br /> <br /> If a character just wants to do what they want, but without disengaging society and following Conscience and Self-Control... That's Humanity all along. It was never defined by not knowing you're a monster, or not accepting it. It's just about following basic social norms.<br /> <br /> On another thread I explained how Humanity in Vampire is a naturalistic morality, not a moral code. It isn't being good in accordance to what a given society says, but in accordance to what life in a society demands to be understood as basic decency. Being imperfect is a part of it, so you shouldn't, in any Path, be required to live as a paragon to be recognized as a follower, less of all Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T22:07:01-07:00","id":1563487,"title":"","content":"I like much of the general concept and theme, but I disagree on the idea that a lack of desire should be considered a sin.<br /> <br /> The path is about pursuing your own True Will, correct? So what happens if the vampire reaches a point where they are content with their lot in life?<br /> <br /> Constantly seeking out new desires to pursue / fulfill sounds more like an obligation, than a genuine expression of True Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T00:00:47-07:00","id":1563489,"title":"","content":"How do they participate in society?<br /> <br /> One of the continuous conflicts for vampires is they can't actually be a part of society. Not being able to do anything during the day, the masquerade, the sects, the jyhad and their own inhuman psychology all raises huge barriers which ultimately makes it impossible.<br /> <br /> Which is actually good for this path in gameplay, gives it an unresolvable problem it will always have to wrestle with. Nice place to explore that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T00:55:29-07:00","id":1563491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563487#post1563487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constantly seeking out new desires to pursue / fulfill sounds more like an obligation, than a genuine expression of True Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Path is ultimately a source of moral obligations, that's kind of the point. But I do agree that the way it's built this seems strange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563489#post1563489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they participate in society?<br /> <br /> One of the continuous conflicts for vampires is they can't actually be a part of society. Not being able to do anything during the day, the masquerade, the sects, the jyhad and their own inhuman psychology all raises huge barriers which ultimately makes it impossible.<br /> <br /> Which is actually good for this path in gameplay, gives it an unresolvable problem it will always have to wrestle with. Nice place to explore that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the books say and, while it is a common interpretation and even Sabbat party line, it isn't by any means absolute truth.<br /> <br /> In any big city you have enough night life for some people to effectively be part of society only at night.<br /> <br /> Neither the Masquerade, Sects or Jyhad place that big of a burden on human interaction, as a vampire only usually needs a few hours per week to deal with such concerns (the reason why immortality causes ennui, not burnout). If you go to Elysium or something every week you are already a very active Member.<br /> <br /> And inhuman psychology is pure fan delusion, no matter how popular. Most books, including all cores, are exceedingly clear that vampires share the same basic psychology and needs as regular people, and even the hunger for blood is directly referred as an addiction. There's not a single aspect of it that isn't intrinsically human, just put in an extraordinary context.<br /> <br /> For those who play like that: almost every and all attempts I've seen to &quot;be inhuman&quot; resulted in something that was painfully human, as the very logic to conclude that would be inhuman behavior was not only human, but pedestrian. I never found a single depiction of a Sabbat that wasn't just one flavor of human disillusionment at best, run of the mill misanthropy other times or just teenager stupidity with great frequency. All those characters still follow strictly human psychology and needs behind their morals and facade (things humans also do).<br /> <br /> Only a few times I've seen anyone really doing a decent job at playing a character with a mind and behavior that don't fit a regular human, and every single one was playing a Changeling, not any other splat.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the wall of text, but this childish &quot;inhuman&quot; bullshit grates me royally and have done so for almost 30 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T02:32:43-07:00","id":1563492,"title":"","content":"I think it maybe problematic for <i>players</i>. Like, RPGs usually have a degree of forward momentum from the ST, so much of the tension of the path gets removed.<br /> <br /> But as an NPC path, I think it could be really interesting. Like, there seems ample opportunity to engage in some really pathological double-think:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563487#post1563487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens if the vampire reaches a point where they are content with their lot in life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not where you want to be? Fairly consistent desires that allow you to live a relatively safe existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Constantly seeking out new desires to pursue / fulfill sounds more like an obligation, than a genuine expression of True Will. </div> </div> </div>I agree, but 'True will' is already pretty questionable as a concept. It just matters that the vampire believes in it.<br /> <br /> From a psychological point of view, perhaps that's the way the path works. The effort the vampire puts into constantly seeking new desires is what allows them to tamp down the beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T03:29:46-07:00","id":1563493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563492#post1563492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that not where you want to be? Fairly consistent desires that allow you to live a relatively safe existence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that the vampire could reach a state in their existence, where they feel content with what they already have, and choose to protect it, instead of trying to expand further.<br /> <br /> As somebody who's getting very close to 40 years old, I've become painfully aware of how exhausting chasing the next interest can be. Doing so for centuries would be mind boggling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563492#post1563492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, but 'True will' is already pretty questionable as a concept. It just matters that the vampire believes in it.<br /> <br /> From a psychological point of view, perhaps that's the way the path works. The effort the vampire puts into constantly seeking new desires is what allows them to tamp down the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way that I personally see it, is that this path could be seen as a form of 'optimistic nihilism.'<br /> <br /> Just because you don't acknowledge any higher authority beyond your own will and desires, that doesn't necessarily mean you have to be a complete ass hole about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T06:13:55-07:00","id":1563496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563491#post1563491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, a Path is ultimately a source of moral obligations, that's kind of the point. But I do agree that the way it's built this seems strange.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not what the books say and, while it is a common interpretation and even Sabbat party line, it isn't by any means absolute truth.<br /> <br /> In any big city you have enough night life for some people to effectively be part of society only at night.<br /> <br /> Neither the Masquerade, Sects or Jyhad place that big of a burden on human interaction, as a vampire only usually needs a few hours per week to deal with such concerns (the reason why immortality causes ennui, not burnout). If you go to Elysium or something every week you are already a very active Member.<br /> <br /> And inhuman psychology is pure fan delusion, no matter how popular. Most books, including all cores, are exceedingly clear that vampires share the same basic psychology and needs as regular people, and even the hunger for blood is directly referred as an addiction. There's not a single aspect of it that isn't intrinsically human, just put in an extraordinary context.<br /> <br /> For those who play like that: almost every and all attempts I've seen to &quot;be inhuman&quot; resulted in something that was painfully human, as the very logic to conclude that would be inhuman behavior was not only human, but pedestrian. I never found a single depiction of a Sabbat that wasn't just one flavor of human disillusionment at best, run of the mill misanthropy other times or just teenager stupidity with great frequency. All those characters still follow strictly human psychology and needs behind their morals and facade (things humans also do).<br /> <br /> Only a few times I've seen anyone really doing a decent job at playing a character with a mind and behavior that don't fit a regular human, and every single one was playing a Changeling, not any other splat.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the wall of text, but this childish &quot;inhuman&quot; bullshit grates me royally and have done so for almost 30 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're overthinking this.<br /> <br /> Inhuman psychology examples:<br /> roll conscience, oh you failed, loose one humanity.<br /> <br /> Oh you visit the Nosferatu warrens: yeah it's covered in old corpses cause they don't care. You don't really either since you know, low humanity vampire.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, the Gangrel lives in the forest since he has protean. He hunts animals and spends most of his time as one. <br /> <br /> Note how none of the above requires roleplay and also all of the above can be asserted by the St. Also they're small, easy to implement, easy to repeat, helps with mood.<br /> <br /> Not so difficult.<br /> <br /> Players can do heavy rp if they want to of course.<br /> <br /> You as the St can literally just assert the dark empty street feels comforting to them. Small tidbits of atmosphere from the st, not high concept rp from the players.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T08:42:18-07:00","id":1563497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563493#post1563493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that the vampire could reach a state in their existence, where they feel content with what they already have, and choose to protect it, instead of trying to expand further.<br /> <br /> As somebody who's getting very close to 40 years old, I've become painfully aware of how exhausting chasing the next interest can be. Doing so for centuries would be mind boggling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's you disagreeing with the Path's philosophy, not the Path having a problem as a Path.<br /> <br /> The goal of a Path is to give the vampire a goal to strive for that demands them to be engaged and mindful of their identity, keeping the Beast at bay with it.<br /> <br /> If you feel it to be exhausting, is because it is. If it weren't, the Beast would make its hold, being logically correct or sound wouldn't stop it. Even Paths that indulge the Beast and follow Instinct are doing so with the goal of keeping a Kindred sane and functional against the alien thing that is trying to turn them into a Wight, the Forever Frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563496#post1563496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're overthinking this.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's a little different.<br /> <br /> TL; DR: I'm saying the game isn't about being inhuman, your examples aren't inhuman, and defining vampires as inhuman is boring when not outright irritating.<br /> <br /> 1. I'm stating the concept is not what the game is about, and it is not what the game is about. You can use it freely, but when you say that the vampire being psychologically inhuman is what the game proposes, that's blatantly false.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm sustaining that things like your examples are not, in fact, anything remotely close to what I'd describe as inhuman psychology. Humanity itself is the only thing close to it, but still it's a very human reaction to resolve dissonance by changing your emotional attachment to moral values or the values themselves. All the others are perfectly human, thinking otherwise is the very point that grates me.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm disinterested of the whole thing. I don't think the themes of decay and degradation that those scenes bring are a problem, I think the association of this with &quot;inhuman&quot; is boring. It's for me the blandest approach possible to the game, and it misses so many actual points of the game to focus on performative edginess that I find the result enormously irritating more often than not.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying vampires shouldn't feel at home among corpses, being alone in the forest or in dark places and so on. I'm not saying themes of morbid degradation aren't part of the game, and a important one. But for one the books are adamant about in the end Vampires feeling the human need for some level of companionship and socializing. It also states through the rules of Humanity that denying such need to wallow in solitude and misanthropy is unhealthy, which is exactly how it is for humans. And finally this has zero to do with &quot;being inhuman&quot;.<br /> <br /> My major problem with the whole inhuman rationale is that more often than not it justify not engaging with moral conflicts rather than making anything interesting with them and overall make for characters like Sasha Vykos, a pointless edgy teenager without any relevant personality behind shock value. It was cool when I was 12. Now it's just repetitive and annoyingly uninspired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T11:28:12-07:00","id":1563503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563497#post1563497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My major problem with the whole inhuman rationale is that more often than not it justify not engaging with moral conflicts rather than making anything interesting with them and overall make for characters like Sasha Vykos, a pointless edgy teenager without any relevant personality behind shock value. It was cool when I was 12. Now it's just repetitive and annoyingly uninspired.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless you're playing in a mixed group, there's not supposed to be any moral conflicts behind a PoE.<br /> <br /> Adopting a Path means adopting an entirely different set of ethics from the Path of Humanity. Your vampire has learned to normalize this kind of edgy behavior, and views it as a completely rational way of thinking. If they did not, then they would have failed when attempting to adopt the Path in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T12:42:56-07:00","id":1563505,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the feedback, this is already very helpful.<br /> <br /> I will try to address and clarify the points you brought up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is basically an awkward Path of What I'd Do Anyway, and one that's literally that, it exists for the character to act freely, without ideology or pressure beyond wanting to do whatever you did. The reason this gap exists isn't negligence, but that Paths were made precisely to not do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. I think I failed to convey an essential part of what True Will encompasses, which is a pretty dramatic failure, since the whole thing is built on it and subsequent rules make no sense without that context.<br /> <br /> I will try to explain by relating to existing Paths. Many of them have a specific role baked into them: ruler, martyr, scholar, monster and so on. Instead of making that role specific, True Will is meant to function as a role that results from the personal desires. It's what people may say is 'their calling', their destined route. Crowley called it the divinely ordained place in the universe, but I want to keep concrete spirituality out as much as possible.<br /> If the desire of a character is for power and they see their calling as a ruler, the Path of Power and the Inner Voice becomes their Path of What I'd Do Anyway. In that sense True Will is a generic placeholder for that. It's very much a long term perspective in stark contrast to short term Wants, although the Path acknowledges that it may change over time.<br /> <br /> The attempt here is to build a framework that supports the restrictions that must emerge from a chosen role. Instead of having &quot;Failing to respect your superiors&quot; as a concrete sin, the sins are meant to facilitate those concrete restrictions when confronted with the Self, the Beast, and Others. You called it naturalistic morality, which is what I'm going for, albeit with a different nature than Humanity. Taking &quot;Do what you will&quot; literal as a license for wanton action is pretty much the opposite of what the Path tries to achieve.<br /> This makes formulating concrete sins difficult, though. There is certainly some struggle with language on my side to convey the right ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, my impression of the whole project is that you're trying to fill a perceived gap without asking what the narrative goal of the Path is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively, the idea is to allow for characters a more flexible role than the existing Paths provide, if they choose to follow a Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hierarchy of Sins has to be clear and objective. Deciding if a sin occurred or not must be as unambiguous as possible, the best case being an objective behavior. That's the greatest challenge with Paths built around open ended goals like &quot;do what you will&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. As you can see, I'm struggling with it. Since you are asking from a player's perspective, I likely can only offer 'roleplay' as an unsatisfying answer to most of the questions that concern the psyche of the character except a select few that have a corresponding mechanic: I will go through the list point by point and explain from the 'perspective' of the Path, that can hopefully help me to condense the hierarchy better. I won't necessarily agree with the truth or validity of those explanations myself, the goal is to make the internal logic coherent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I can't know if the character want something for themselves. I can see if what they desire is the desire of the Beast of another, but not if no other motivation exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motivation of a desire is, at this level, not a restriction: Inevitably, all desire is created through interaction with the world and others, but a desire created <i>in you</i> is distinct from a desire in another. Even a shared desire with another is distinct because it resides in a different place (yourself). A desire awoken by the Beast that is not the Beast's own, or a desire inspired by another are raw material. Making it truly your own (or not) is covered by the second step.<br /> The cardinal sin is apathy, having no motivation besides base necessities and serving the desires of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563487#post1563487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The path is about pursuing your own True Will, correct? So what happens if the vampire reaches a point where they are content with their lot in life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fulfillment does not mean being devoid of desire, it means you are able to satisfy your current desires. You will probably want to add sustaining this fulfillment as a new desire, which starts a recursion (that is wanted).<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character's desires, motivations, and reason for existence have been thoroughly corrupted, abandoned, or suppressed to the point where they merely exist as a shell. This also triggers as result of a Discipline or other manipulation of the mind that causes this state temporarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. How can I say if a character understand their own desire of not? How can I distinguish the mistake between instinct/desire or conformity/will and legitimate overlap, especially in a Path that teaches precisely the need for indulgence of the Beast's desires and following of social norms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Introspection. A new desire must be examined to decide if it is something you truly want, or whether it needs to be adapted or abandoned. Where does it come from? Why does it exist? What are the consequences if you follow this desire? This would be a truly daunting task if it would happen in a vacuum, but it does not: it is a recursive process in which the new desire is contrasted with the existing True Will, and a decision must be made to either integrate or abandon it. Integration means that the True Will changes, or rather, evolves: the decision is carefully made with consideration whether it is detrimental or beneficial to the long term realization of the Will. Overlap is natural and actually helps with that process - if a new desire caused by conformity harmonizes with the True Will, all the better.<br /> This does not cover the experience itself. Spontaneous reaction to a new desire is hard to control and covered later on the Path.<br /> The sin is sustaining a new desire without the process of reflection and integration.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character, after experiencing a new desire, keeps following that desire without stopping to reflect on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. How can I access the character's will to say when it's being stifled vs followed?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one builds on the previous step: if your True Will is the core of yourself, acting against it is detrimental by definition. Conversely, you know something to be detrimental or stifling if it is against your Will. Since acting in accordance with your True Will comes naturally, this happens mostly by force - by your Beast or from the outside. If you cannot justify acting against your Will momentarily by being able to better act <i>with</i> it in the long run, you are betraying yourself. When you find yourself in moral agreement with a rule that runs clearly against the codified rules of your Will, then you are in crisis and need to re-evaluate the rules that make up your Will.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character is forced to act against themselves, or worse, they deliberately sabotage themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Those work well when the Path gives clear parameters for what you should seek, but when the point is one's own will I can't say if it was lost or not, if submitting the Beast is necessary or if appeasement of another is submission or desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is perhaps the most literal one and it can be tracked with stats. Hopefully the previous explanations have been enough to establish that the clear parameters are defined by the Will itself, this sin is concerned with maintenance.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: Losing a permanent point of Willpower, running out of temporary Willpower. Losing a Virtue. Not spending Willpower when resisting the Beast. Becoming blood-bound, or not trying to resist Domination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Unless you define this one as any dice roll failure, the problem again is that all of those rely on knowing beforehand what the character will or desire. If I didn't act, who can say I willed otherwise? Who can say I didn't will my Beast to do what it did? If my desire is to harm those of others, then what?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned before, Will is not made up on the spot. It is a gradual development and as tangible as the paradigm of any other Path, and as a consequence, becomes a more predictable role. Who can say whether a decision was caused by opportunity or by Will? The player, hopefully.<br /> The &quot;Denying others their desires unless they harm yours&quot; needs to go, though. I'm going to replace that with &quot;refusal to share in your desires, if asked&quot;. The sin is forfeiting opportunities to strengthen and nurture the desires that are the basis of your Will.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character refuses an opportunity to engage in their chosen role, or misses the opportunity to let the Beast act in that role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. Those are antithetical to your stipulations: I can't evolve my desires if I can't be tainted by the desires if others. I can't accept and indulge the Beast without letting it influence me. I can't associate with people without a risk of having my desires regularly fouled. This is nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are not against change per-se, the quality of that change matters. A change that is integratable into or harmonizes with the paradigm is welcome, a change that would weaken the desires it stands on is not. Taint and befoulment are not value-neutral words; evolving the Will is going forward, not backwards. You should be able to judge when the influence of another person makes your psyche less healthy - yes, this is sometimes too subtle to notice, but that is exactly what the rule is trying to prevent. The sin is letting others weaken your Will, or allowing it to degrade rather than improve it.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character is put in serious doubt about the soundness and validity of the desires or rules that build their Will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. Demand to expand, indulge and engage with society, without recognizing they can clash. It's one thing for a Path to demand two conflicting goals for you to find a balance, it's another for it to be unaware of the conflict to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one seems to have caused the most misunderstandings.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563487#post1563487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constantly seeking out new desires to pursue / fulfill sounds more like an obligation, than a genuine expression of True Will.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563492#post1563492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effort the vampire puts into constantly seeking new desires is what allows them to tamp down the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, &quot;Failing to explore a new desire&quot; does not necessarily mean actively seeking out new desires - that is a possibility, but the more likely scenario is that you find yourself confronted with a new desire you need to examine. This rule just means you <i>must</i> examine it (as per the explanation of the second sin), and are not allowed to simply ignore it - because it may turn out to be a valuable addition to your construct of Will. You can not know until you have considered it. Likewise, categorically dismissing any desires of the Beast will not only waste finding possibly compatible building blocks, it also dismisses opportunities to soothe it by satisfying shared desires. Finally, refusing to engage with society excludes you from encountering new desires, as well as of robbing yourself of the opportunity to share in them. Conflict is kind of the point, as it requires re-examination and re-validation of your Will.<br /> The sin is categorically refusing to confront your Will with new desires to temper it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563489#post1563489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they participate in society?</div> </div> </div> </div>@monteparnas already expanded on this, but I will add that society does not only mean personal, inter-human society. Your circle of online friends and this forum are societal structures. Clan is a society, Sects are a society. The Nest full of Baali is a society. Social ethics will vary vastly between them, but the social construct is still there.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character isolates or deprivates themselves from experiencing new desires, or is forced to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. The description doesn't follow prescription. I can apply if I interpret it as &quot;harming anyone by accident&quot;, but the description indicates this is not the intention. Again, it relies on knowing beforehand a will from the character that can be anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is - hopefully - too resolved by understanding that Will is not &quot;anything&quot;, but a defined role with rules. Harm is meant as literal as it is metaphorical, and to put it bluntly, just means to not shit in the bed you made. There are situations where you will not be able to avoid it, as with being forced to act against your Will. There will be conflicts of interest, conflicts of ethics, and more.<br /> The sin is to provoke conflict with your Will. And no, if your desire is provoking conflict as part of your True Will to become the Best Evil Vizier, it's not that conflict.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character causes a situation in which their role is imperiled to be damaged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9. How can I say an action occurred without will? How do I measure self reflection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acting instinctively is a mechanic: R\u00f6tschreck, Frenzy. It obviously does not cover something like reflexively catching a ball. But acting impulsively without thinking also counts. If the motivation for an action was 'because I felt like it', and not a deliberate choice as in 'it was in line with my Will' we are back to the literal 'Do what you want' and not the 'Do what you are'. Every action causes an equal and opposite reaction, and this reaction is socially expressed through your associates. It will reveal how implementing your Will is received from the outside, and how society perceives you. It gives you an outside evaluation of yourself, and in turn should affect your decision on how to evolve your Will further.<br /> The sin is acting thoughtless, or letting instinct take hold of you.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character acts spontaneously, without thought of consequences. Falling into R\u00f6tschreck or Frenzy, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563486#post1563486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. This is the only one close to be actionable and still requires to assess feelings that may be masked for any reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masking those feelings is fine. The point is that experiencing those feelings should alert you to questioning whether what you do is really your Will, or whether your Will is covering enough of your ethics to not cause these feelings in the first place.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: Should be obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That.. is a lot more text than I anticipated. This will be difficult to condense down into coherent, meaningful sins that can transport all that. I understand that this is a lot more complex than existing Paths, but at the same time, I don't think it is <i>that</i> complex for a personal philosophy. I still may have to consider dumbing it down a bit, simply for functionality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T13:34:03-07:00","id":1563506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563505#post1563505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> already expanded on this, but I will add that society does not only mean personal, inter-human society. Your circle of online friends and this forum are societal structures. Clan is a society, Sects are a society. The Nest full of Baali is a society. Social ethics will vary vastly between them, but the social construct is still there.<br /> <br /> Mechanism: The character isolates or deprivates themselves from experiencing new desires, or is forced to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good clarification to make, I think it's easy to read society as the place you live in. Still could use a bit more, because this would be a good way to insert your path into an actual game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T14:20:12-07:00","id":1563507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563505#post1563505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will try to explain by relating to existing Paths. <b>Many of them have a specific role baked into them: ruler, martyr, scholar, monster and so on. Instead of making that role specific, True Will is meant to function as a role that results from the personal desires.</b> It's what people may say is 'their calling', their destined route. Crowley called it the divinely ordained place in the universe, but I want to keep concrete spirituality out as much as possible.<br /> <br /> If the desire of a character is for power and they see their calling as a ruler, the Path of Power and the Inner Voice becomes their Path of What I'd Do Anyway. In that sense True Will is a generic placeholder for that. It's very much a long term perspective in stark contrast to short term Wants, although the Path acknowledges that it may change over time.<br /> <br /> The attempt here is to build a framework that supports the restrictions that must emerge from a chosen role. Instead of having &quot;Failing to respect your superiors&quot; as a concrete sin, the sins are meant to facilitate those concrete restrictions when confronted with the Self, the Beast, and Others. You called it naturalistic morality, which is what I'm going for, albeit with a different nature than Humanity. Taking &quot;Do what you will&quot; literal as a license for wanton action is pretty much the opposite of what the Path tries to achieve.<br /> This makes formulating concrete sins difficult, though. There is certainly some struggle with language on my side to convey the right ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolding mine, to highlight what I think is an important part of the problem here.<br /> <br /> You've noted how many of the pre-existing Paths are aimed towards a particular kind of role, but I think a better way to put it might be to say that they are all directed at some kind of ideal, principle, or Mission. Whatever the new role or value that the Path espouses, its purpose is to provide something as an alternative to Humanity that keeps the Beast from running too wild. Even the Road/Path of the Beast places certain specific ideological constraints upon the Vampire that follows it, despite giving the Beast some freedom to run wild being a central part of how the Path is supposed to operate.<br /> <br /> Where your Path runs into trouble is that it has no Mission. The Path doesn't lead anywhere; you haven't made a Path as much as potential framework for a Path. And I think that's part of why your explanations for what qualifies as a Sin for each level of the Hierarchy ends up getting so convoluted: you don't have a clear Mission or Principle to point at, and are instead trying to describe a complicated framework that will permit you to do the equivalent of a Find+Replace by just inserting whatever values you decide to give the character that can fit into that framework.<br /> <br /> I also think that lack of a clear defining Mission is also a failure of the Path from a Watsonian perspective. This Path is so flexible and conditional that I don't think it would actually work to help keep the Beast under control. I think a functional Path needs one or two things from its Mission: a guiding principle that the Vampire can aim at by following the Path, or boundaries that the Vampire must stay within to follow the Path. Without some combination of those two features, the Path won't be able to functionally replace the norms of Humanity by giving the Vampire a standard to adhere to beyond the impulses of the Beast.<br /> <br /> I personally think you should focus less on trying to create one Uber-Path that can cover countless roles, and instead be more willing to make multiple specific Paths suited for the specific roles you feel that the current Paths aren't covering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T14:35:49-07:00","id":1563508,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> Oh, that's another thing, finding a way to shape your desires in a way that makes them compatible with society. That fundamentally can not be an expression of True Will, because you are conforming to societal expectations. You are allowing society to dictate what desires are acceptable to pursue, and which must be rejected.<br /> <br /> True Will, by its very concept, does not allow for compromise. Because compromise implies that you must capitulate to the demands of someone else in order to get something you want. And for a Path that evolved from the Road of Sin, that doesn't seem like something they'd approve of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T15:09:13-07:00","id":1563509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563503#post1563503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're playing in a mixed group, there's not supposed to be any moral conflicts behind a PoE.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wrong in several ways.<br /> <br /> A Path is meant to change moral conflicts, not to eliminate them. That's why it has a Hierarchy of Sins. The whole point as design is to allow for characters that don't work under Humanity, but still give them moral conflicts to engage with. A Path follower is also a moral play by contrast, which is engaging with morality.<br /> <br /> When the character has to chose between their wishes, safety or convenience and following an ideology as represented by a Path, when they ponder about how the Path changed them or how it puts them in a role that compliments the roles of mortals in the grand scheme, when they feel doubt (which is something they face, the whole point of the rules is that), all those are but a few examples of how a character can follow an alternative moral framework and still that be a way for the player to engage with a moral conflict.<br /> <br /> In the books where they're presented, the goal of using them as tools for moral examination without making the character follow a regular morality, and above all the intention that Paths will still challenge the characters morally even if through their own perspectives, are blatantly clear and directly stated more than once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563505#post1563505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that this is a lot more complex than existing Paths, but at the same time, I don't think it is <i>that</i> complex for a personal philosophy. I still may have to consider dumbing it down a bit, simply for functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will have to change it somewhat, yes. And thanks for the clarification, and I can get the Crowleyan vibe you warned about.<br /> <br /> While they clarified, the answers didn't solve any of the questions for a reason I myself am at fault of not being clear on: they tell how the Seeker will know the answer, but I'm not the Seeker.<br /> <br /> That's the central conundrum: a Path must be observable to function in the game. The player is not a follower, nor is the ST, and likely aren't philosophers either. Nor is a game trait the place to give a proper philosophy lesson, even if it is solidly built over one. You need a set of guidelines that anyone can use and say if that character followed suit or not.<br /> <br /> Relying exclusively on the player's awareness and good faith is another big no. It fly in some groups, but will be severely problematic and understandably so in others. Finally, defining a Path's proper behavior as a character stopping to start an examination monologue all the time is not going to work out well.<br /> <br /> Functionality requires those three: following a Path must be an observable, unambiguous act that any observer can understand and judge by themselves, and this behavior must be fitting for gameplay.<br /> <br /> One Path I think you can take a look at is the Revised Eastern Path of Paradox they made in the last Ravnos Clanbook for the vampires of India. It has a similar premise of personalized goal in the form of a Svadharma, a fated role to fulfill, so to speak. It solves the problem adding to the Path a formalization process: you're first seeking to learn your Dharma, which you solve between you and the ST, and once you have that your personal Dharma is the anchor of the Path<br /> <br /> Calling it a rule is too much, but is unnecessary, the point is for the step to be there. What your Path needs to work within your premises and goals is that, a process to formalize individual Will and for how and when to revise it.<br /> <br /> Another option within your goals may be to change this into a Path creation system rather than a fleshed out Path. Not only as a resource for STs who want to introduce new Paths, but a framework for players who want to engage the character in-game in the process of developing and testing a Path, something Sabbat scholars are known to engage in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T03:58:59-07:00","id":1563529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563508#post1563508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That fundamentally can not be an expression of True Will, because you are conforming to societal expectations. You are allowing society to dictate what desires are acceptable to pursue, and which must be rejected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is social conformity not itself a legitimate desire?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think 'True Will' is a pretty incoherent concept fullstop. Unless you have a metaphysical structure for it (like a holy guardian angel or what have you), on what basis are we distinguishing true will from other desires? The whole thing is quite Socratic, which I don't think many people have ever really found terribly convincing.<br /> <br /> However, I don't think it matters. Basically all the paths have some degree of incoherence and bad faith. What matters is whether it works or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for a Path that evolved from the Road of Sin, that doesn't seem like something they'd approve of. </div> </div> </div>I mean, they almost certainly don't. They presumably treat the PoDaTW as a wishy-washy version of their own path.<br /> <br /> That's good though. It's built-in social conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T05:08:12-07:00","id":1563530,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm giving this a once-over. Apologies for not replying with quotes directly, I took all your feedback into consideration, which has been very helpful.<br /> <br /> Changes:<br /> - Dropped Meta-Path attempt, too complex and unwieldy. Not what I was trying to do anyway.<br /> - Removed True Will entirely from Sins and instead made it the aspiration of the Path<br /> - Removed elements that tried to put the spiritual aspect into rules<br /> - Added elements of P.o. Self-Focus, Metamorphosis, Entelechy, Eastern Paradox<br /> - Un-Crowleyfied description<br /> - Stronger emphasis on uncompromising nature<br /> - Removed redundant Sins and those logically facilitated by other Sins<br /> - Narrowed and rearranged Sins to more stringent progression<br /> - Adjusted phrasing to be in line with existing Paths<br /> - Reworked Rationales<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Path of Desire and True Will (V2)</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The origins of this Path can be traced back to the much older Road of Sin. There are key differences though: while it identifies desire as the driving force of both Beast and vampire, it tries to balance the egocentrism of the Road by integrating it with society. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The followers of the Path seek True Will, a concept that is a combination of destiny, mindful action, and harmonic integration in the world all at once, while also placing utmost importance on the realization of the self. An adherent will strive to attain this state by refining themselves in a way not unlike a Metamorphisist would experiment with and refine their body, but will instead weigh their desires against themselves, their Beast, and society.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Aspirants tend to combine introspection and self-reflection with living out their passions: in order to find their True Will, they have to engage with new ideas and conflicts both mundane and spiritual to temper themselves while staying true on their path to their destined place in the world. On the other hand, they need to have clear vision of where they see themselves, in the present and future, as well as a strong will to push for that vision.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Much greater emphasis is put on control of the Beast than was usual for the Road of Sin. The Beast is a part of themselves adherents must find a common ground with, but set strict lines that cannot be crossed. There is no reason to deny the Beast pleasure in feeding, or indulgence in other desires \u2013 but there can be no quarter if the urges would imperil their progress on the Path. This stick-and-carrot approach eschews compromise, as with most else of the Path.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Path attempts to mediate realization of the self (Courage) with the Beast (Self-Control) and society (Conscience). In game terms, True Will closely corresponds to the character concept and the goals of the player on where to lead them. The player should have a clear idea of what those goals are, and what their character aspires to be.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Virtues:</b> Conscience, Self-Control</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ethics:</b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Act mindful. All your actions will be reflected back onto you. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Beast belongs to you, but you do not belong to it.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Share in your desires, but refuse unwanted ones. Never compromise.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Freedom, control, and will are your most valuable tools. Do not lose them.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is no growth on toxic soil. Cultivate your environment as you would yourself.</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Hierarchy of Sins</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Path of Desire and True Will</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rating</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Moral Guideline</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rationale</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">10</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Feeling guilt for your actions</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There can be no guilt in mindful action</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">9</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failing to explore a new desire</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Desire is kindling, do not let it run out</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">8</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Refusing indulgence that harms none</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Desire needs to burn to placate the Beast</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">7</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Refusing an opportunity to share in your passions</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Do not waste what is freely given to you</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">6</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure to treat others as you would be treated</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There can be no harmony in imbalance</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Acting against your own self interests</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Always evaluate, but never compromise</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Succumbing to Frenzy</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Beast does not control, it obeys</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Becoming blood bound</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Your freedom is your greatest tool</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Losing Will or Virtue</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Your will is your strongest resource</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Apathy</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Losing desire is to embrace final death</span></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T05:53:03-07:00","id":1563531,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> Not for everyone. Not for those who wish to make their mark on the world, and especially not for those of the Punk culture to which World of Darkness originally appealed to. Raging against societal norms is pretty much the entire premise of what Punk is all about.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the subject of what constitutes True Will, the simple answer to that is you pursue the desire because you genuinely believe that it is worth pursuing. You're not doing it because some outside influence tells you that it has value, and the opposite applies to rejection of said desire. You reject it, because you personally have no interest in such a desire. Not because society tells you that such a desire is dangerous or reprehensible.<br /> <br /> <br /> True Will is exactly that, <b>true will.</b> It's you making decisions based on your own genuine beliefs and feelings, uncontaminated by cultural biases or social engineering.<br /> <br /> If a vampire on this path refrains from eating babies, it's not because society tells them that eating babies is monstrously abhorrent. It's because the vampire in question has no desire to eat babies.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> As far as the root concept goes, I think this path has some decent potential. But it's philosophy could still use a bit more tweaking. Because in its current state, it tenets contradict themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T07:58:35-07:00","id":1563534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563531#post1563531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the root concept goes, I think this path has some decent potential. But it's philosophy could still use a bit more tweaking. Because in its current state, it tenets contradict themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point them out for me? I may have been looking at it too long and may be blind to obvious contradictions by now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563531#post1563531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of what constitutes True Will, the simple answer to that is you pursue the desire because you genuinely believe that it is worth pursuing. You're not doing it because some outside influence tells you that it has value, and the opposite applies to rejection of said desire. You reject it, because you personally have no interest in such a desire. Not because society tells you that such a desire is dangerous or reprehensible.<br /> <br /> True Will is exactly that, <b>true will.</b> It's you making decisions based on your own genuine beliefs and feelings, uncontaminated by cultural biases or social engineering.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is all true, but it does in no way preclude agreeing with social norms either. It's not contrarian for the sake of it, only when there is an incompatibility.<br /> <br /> It's not a compromise to accept agreeable ethics and reject others. As long as the decision lies with the individual whether to accept them or not, it does not impede their freedom. That only happens with enforcement of rules they disagree with, or fear thereof - the compromise is when they accept incompatible ethics for the sake of conformity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T08:41:15-07:00","id":1563536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563534#post1563534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you point them out for me? I may have been looking at it too long and may be blind to obvious contradictions by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was for the original write up. You seem to have corrected or addressed them in the more recent version you just posted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563534#post1563534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is all true, but it does in no way preclude agreeing with social norms either. It's not contrarian for the sake of it, only when there is an incompatibility.<br /> <br /> It's not a compromise to accept agreeable ethics and reject others. As long as the decision lies with the individual whether to accept them or not, it does not impede their freedom. That only happens with enforcement of rules they disagree with, or fear thereof - the compromise is when they accept incompatible ethics for the sake of conformity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and the problem was the original write up presented seemed to imply that the follower was expected to make those kinds of compromises, as opposed to willfully choosing to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T08:59:34-07:00","id":1563537,"title":"","content":"This gives me some Cult of Ecstasy vibes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T09:13:08-07:00","id":1563539,"title":"","content":"I think you've done a much better job of putting the Hierarchy of Sins in tangible terms. But I can see where <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> is coming from when he comments on it contradicting itself in places. Unless you are building a condition into the concept of &quot;self-interest&quot; that excludes exploiting others from being a viable option, then the Sins at Rank 5 and 6 are going to constantly contradict one another, where you'll constantly be forced to choose between committing the Sin of treating others different from how you would want to be treated or the Sin of acting against your own self-interest.<br /> <br /> I also think that the Sin at Rank 6, basically &quot;the Golden Rule,&quot; is doing <b>a lot</b> of heavy lifting. Depending on how you conceptualize it, that could be half or more of the Sins listed under Humanity, including some of the really nasty stuff like rape and murder. And you have it at Rank 6. Everything below it is largely the sort of stuff that a character is going to obviously want to avoid, like Frenzy and the Blood Bond. There were some things that I didn't include in my previous post because I was having trouble formulating my thoughts, but fortunately <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> kind of covered it. The Sins on a Path are meant to produce tension and drama in the form of moral conflict. You'll notice that most of the lower ranking Sins in Humanity's Hierarchy are extreme, but definitely not outside the bounds of what could be expected from PC murder-hoboery. I'm not enough of an expert on all of the Paths to be able to say whether they're all appropriately &quot;balanced&quot; in this way, but I can say that some of the ones I've looked at more, like Metamorphosis and Death and the Soul, introduce their own forms of drama by making it a serious Sin to avoid certain forms of antisocial or potentially self-destructive behaviour, like &quot;showing compassion&quot; or &quot;preventing death&quot; or &quot;putting yourself at risk if necessary for SCIENCE.&quot; It's fundamentally different from a system that reflects more typical societal norms like Humanity does, but it still places demands on the role-player. Suddenly, a heart-wrenching description of an injured kitten becomes a moral drama for your character/player, to see whether or not they resist the urge to go &quot;Aw&quot; and try to rescue the poor animal, which would be a Sin.<br /> <br /> I just want to quickly note that having &quot;Apathy&quot; be the ultimate Sin for this Path really doesn't work if you intend it to be available for PCs, who are by their nature highly driven and calculating in their actions. To the extent that Sinning against this kind of tenet is possible, it's the sort of thing that would likely be happening off-screen, not during roleplaying sessions with an engaged and attentive player. This is a Path that a PC cannot fail during play, effectively.<br /> <br /> I do also want to address the points being made about how &quot;True Will&quot; conflicts with the efforts to make the Path more pro-social. This Path is supposed to be descended from the Road of Sin, but supposedly rejects the &quot;egocentrism&quot; of its predecessor. I think the problem with that is that Egocentrism is The Mission of the Road of Sin. That is part of how it staves off the Beast, along with most Paths of the Road adopting Instincts and giving the Beast more freedom. The way you frame the position just seems to take for granted that the Egocentrism of the Road of Sin is a Bug, when it's supposed to be a Feature, and I don't think you've provided an adequate philosophical justification for that rejection, or an explanation for how &quot;True Will&quot; functions as an alternative to Egocentrism as a way to stave off the Beast. It still feels too nebulous when the Egocentrism that supposedly influences it, and presumably serves as its guiding principle, has been hobbled by pro-social compromises, and has also rejected the compromise with the Beast that is implicit in the adoption of Instinct as a Virtue. <br /> <br /> Of course, you've also mentioned the influence of the Path of the Devil, which is somewhat distinct. But there is still an important distinction between it and the Path you've created. To the extent that the Path of the Devil replaces the pure Egocentrism of the Road of Sin with a wider Liberationism, it still has a clear and identifiable Mission that it is aimed at, and the nature of that Mission informs the restrictions that it places upon the Vampire that follows it. And it thus informs the drama that it adds to that character's story.<br /> <br /> And while I've kind of touched on this indirectly, I notice that this Path retains both of the Virtues normally associated with Humanity. Why is that? I know that some of the medieval Roads allowed Vampires to retain both of their original Virtues, but IIRC those were the Roads of Heaven and Humanity, which obviously most closely adhere to the sorts of standards we would associate with modern-day Humanity. This Path supposedly descends from the Road of Sin, but possesses neither of the Virtues associated with it. The Path does not seem to be particularly proud of its ancestry, as most of the discussion around it seems to involve criticism of it. It feels like you want to claim the exaltation of Desire associated with the Road of Sin while rejecting the challenges that following that principle to its logical conclusion would entail for a Vampire living in the modern world.<br /> <br /> Does this really need to be its own Path of Enlightenment, or is it just a philosophy that a Vampire still on the &quot;Path&quot; of Humanity can adhere to in their nightly unlife?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T12:54:33-07:00","id":1563544,"title":"","content":"Version 2 is solid.<br /> <br /> Apathy is the hardest to measure, but for a Level 1 Sin I think it's ok, it should be easy to dismiss and pretty obvious when in a level that warrants a roll.<br /> <br /> Losing traits isn't my personal cup of tea, but not a terrible thing for Level 2, and the others are pretty straightforward to judge but leaving the needed room for interpretation.<br /> <br /> I also like that now the player and ST have good reason to discuss the character's goals. Instead of asking moment to moment analysis, the sins naturally require a clear picture from the get go, in a way a 5 minutes conversation can already go a long way into addressing.<br /> <br /> No complaints I can think of right now, would allow no problem, possibly try as player, and I think it's would be interesting and genuinely distinct.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a>, True Will in philosophical conceptualization has more plastic definitions. There's no consensus among scholars about what it is, how to define or measure, or where to draw the line between legitimate influence and stifling it. And since Paths are philosophy experiments, it's fitting for one to flirt with any nonconventional interpretation.<br /> <br /> Punk isn't aimless subversion, either. It has a vision and a reason behind what it subverts. It is specifically meant as a response to norms that directly or indirectly marginalize people or that enshrine tradition over equality and/or the common good.<br /> <br /> Rebellion for its own sake is being a Poser, and few things are more abhorrent to a Punk than a Poser. Living like a conformist isn't one of them if you're aware of that and is willing to accept challenge and share with other Punks.<br /> <br /> When you add to this that the setting being Punk isn't the same as every character being Punk, it's perfectly valid to have a Path that has a definition of True Will that accepts societal norms as a possible expression, or even that defines True Will by its ability to incorporate such norms. A Path needs internal coherence, not to fit a particular definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T00:07:42-07:00","id":1563558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563529#post1563529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they almost certainly don't. They presumably treat the PoDaTW as a wishy-washy version of their own path.<br /> <br /> That's good though. It's built-in social conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I'm sure they would. One thing I will say is that the Roads tend to be a lot more flexible than modern Paths in regards to the personality of the character; Road of Sin in particular makes little demands on how a follower expresses the tenets, at least before you get down a specific Path of it. That small box on how to play a Sinner in VDA20 which mirrors your sentiment on how a self-centered Path can still be quite social was one of the main motivations to bring that to a modern Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563537#post1563537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gives me some Cult of Ecstasy vibes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not surprising since it has some outright ecstatic tenets. Might also be a result of the thelemic elements still coming through; in-universe Crowley even was a Cult of Ecstasy member before being Embraced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563544#post1563544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apathy is the hardest to measure, but for a Level 1 Sin I think it's ok, it should be easy to dismiss and pretty obvious when in a level that warrants a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think it should be clear a cardinal sin called Apathy doesn't mean having a night when the character doesn't feel like getting out of the coffin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563544#post1563544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing traits isn't my personal cup of tea, but not a terrible thing for Level 2, and the others are pretty straightforward to judge but leaving the needed room for interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get you. For this specific Path, Willpower becomes a bit of an additional Virtue though, and I wanted to at least tie that into the degradation process somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563544#post1563544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No complaints I can think of right now, would allow no problem, possibly try as player, and I think it's would be interesting and genuinely distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> Really appreciate the support from all of you, that would have been a lot harder without it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T03:40:35-07:00","id":1563560,"title":"","content":"Roads occupy a distinct niche in the game. Overall I think they're a superior rule if you want to leave out the theme of Humanity as focus.<br /> <br /> In normal VtM Humanity is basic decency, it is restrictive in a sense, but allows for almost any character concept since you're not required to &quot;follow&quot; it, it's just there.<br /> <br /> Since the point of the game is to explore this, a Path can't be just an alternative, but a contrast, something that reinforces how far a character must go to compensate and be clear they're an extremist. In a sense, the Path is not protection against degeneration, but a less horrible way to degenerate, a psychological damage control.<br /> <br /> Humanity is by design the superior option, even if the character can't recognize it.<br /> <br /> But Dark Ages wanted to explore the contrast of values of medieval societies compared to the modern world. It's not about vampires who try to ditch their human identity, but the world before the Enlightenment and conflict between different social values.<br /> <br /> This had two effects. The first to attend to the need of a more flexible system since there was no expected standard to cover most character concepts. The second to make Roads as stand ins for the social conflicts in the game, as each Road also represents a culture, religion, caste and other social divisions clashing in the world.<br /> <br /> A chronicle devised to displace the notion of a basic natural morality from focus, remove the centrality of human identity from the game and instead work seriously with vampires following different worldviews either as holdover of their living days or response to their condition can do worse than using Roads instead of Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T08:13:24-07:00","id":1563596,"title":"","content":"Since my previous post remains banished to the Shadow Realm for reasons I don't understand, I'm going to share some of the thoughts I've had since posting it, along with a bit of a summary of the key points behind those ideas, but there's a lot of details I just can't be bothered to repeat when I'm just waiting for the mods to approve them &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> OOC I think there's a problem with the Hierarchy of Sins you've constructed, collectively, where they remove or fail to reintroduce a lot of the drama and tension that playing a PoE is supposed to bring to the game, IMO. Most of the lower-ranking Sins are choices your character is already going to want to obviously avoid, so you haven't created tension in the form of a dilemma, but have instead just added additional weight and consequences to things that already tend to be Bad, like Frenzies and Blood Bonds. Again, the choices might make sense individually, but in the big picture they add up to is a Path that kind of looks like Easy-Mode to me.<br /> <br /> In particular, I think having &quot;Treat others as you want to be treated&quot; as your Rank 6 Sin basically front-loads most of the crimes that would trigger rolls on Humanity (theft, assault, murder, etc.) into one single slot on the Hierarchy, and its positioned within the &quot;comfort zone&quot; of Humanity/Path Ratings, that 5-7 area that's considered VERY typical to end up in during play. I also think that the &quot;Golden Rule&quot; does frequently come into conflict with your Rank 5 Sin, &quot;acting against your own Self-Interest,&quot; because there will often be conflicts between the Self-Interest of a Vampire and the well-being and dignity of those around them. Unless you have a very particular definition of Self-Interest, or a very wild concept of &quot;how I would like to be treated&quot; that really needs some elaboration, these two things do seem somewhat contradictory to me.<br /> <br /> Just going to briefly mention that I have a completely opposite opinion of &quot;Apathy&quot; as a Sin. I think it belongs in the 8-10 range where most &quot;thought-crime&quot; Sins typically get put, and that Apathy specifically is a *terrible* choice for a Rank 1 Sin on a Path intended for players to use. See Missing Post for details.<br /> <br /> I also think there's an IC problem where the philosophy of &quot;True Will&quot; remains somewhat vague and non-committal from a philosophical or ideological point of view, and I think that lack of firm convictions would leave it too weak to resist the degrading influence of the Beast. I think you need to commit more to a particular direction, in one of a few possible ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Stop trying to make a Path of Enlightenment. Instead, come up with a more general philosophy that a Vampire can follow in the Unlife while still ultimately being on the &quot;Path&quot; of Humanity. This isn't meant as critically as it possibly sounds: I found myself in a similar position a while ago, where I ended up deciding that my &quot;family-friendly&quot; Tzimisce character concept was better off as someone *influenced* by Metamorphosist thought while not being on the Path of Metamorphosis themself, instead retaining their Humanity.<br /> <br /> 2) Commit to the Egocentrism. Get rid of the &quot;treat others as they want to be treated&quot; nonsense. &quot;Do As Thou Wilt&quot; *is* the sum of the Law. As you discussed above, there is ample discussion of how you can follow the Road of Sin and still be an &quot;enlightened egoist&quot; who understands the need to be nice to other people *when* it suits their own interests. As long as you have Self-Control to manage your Frenzies, and your Path tenets aren't actively pushing you into antisocial behaviour, your Vampire doesn't need to *actually* care about being fair to others.<br /> <br /> 3) Abandon the Egocentrism. Stop trying to use the Road of Sin as your guide, because it just doesn't play well with a Path that wants to have serious moral obligations to other people. You might want to use the Path of Entelechy as a example of a Path that is more pro-Humanity and pro-Self-Control as a means of pursuing self-actualization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T10:21:31-07:00","id":1563600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563596#post1563596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOC I think there's a problem with the Hierarchy of Sins you've constructed, collectively, where they remove or fail to reintroduce a lot of the drama and tension that playing a PoE is supposed to bring to the game, IMO. Most of the lower-ranking Sins are choices your character is already going to want to obviously avoid, so you haven't created tension in the form of a dilemma, but have instead just added additional weight and consequences to things that already tend to be Bad, like Frenzies and Blood Bonds. Again, the choices might make sense individually, but in the big picture they add up to is a Path that kind of looks like Easy-Mode to me.<br /> <br /> In particular, I think having &quot;Treat others as you want to be treated&quot; as your Rank 6 Sin basically front-loads most of the crimes that would trigger rolls on Humanity (theft, assault, murder, etc.) into one single slot on the Hierarchy, and its positioned within the &quot;comfort zone&quot; of Humanity/Path Ratings, that 5-7 area that's considered VERY typical to end up in during play. I also think that the &quot;Golden Rule&quot; does frequently come into conflict with your Rank 5 Sin, &quot;acting against your own Self-Interest,&quot; because there will often be conflicts between the Self-Interest of a Vampire and the well-being and dignity of those around them. Unless you have a very particular definition of Self-Interest, or a very wild concept of &quot;how I would like to be treated&quot; that really needs some elaboration, these two things do seem somewhat contradictory to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! I consider the conflict between Self, Beast, and Society to be the main difficulty you feel is missing, and in particular the the conflict between Rank 5 / 6 Sins. I don't see them as a direct contradiction though:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Treat others as you would be treated</span>\u200b&quot; comes directly from the Path of Self-Focus, which is <i>very</i> self-centered. The reason is that the moral judgement lies with the character, and not an external list of ethics. It also does not mean it is 'nice'; the flip-side and implicit result is &quot;eye for an eye&quot; when it comes to enforcement of those judgements.<br /> Unfortunately, I think it is impossible to make a list of Sins that is both playable and sufficiently nuanced, at least with my command of English. IMO &quot;Becoming blood bound&quot; should imply that loss of autonomy in general is considered a bad thing and something like authoritarian rules are at the very least suspect.<br /> <br /> But if that isn't the case, then the description and general Ethics do not cover enough of those nuances. I will have another look whether I can include some more specifics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563596#post1563596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going to briefly mention that I have a completely opposite opinion of &quot;Apathy&quot; as a Sin. I think it belongs in the 8-10 range where most &quot;thought-crime&quot; Sins typically get put, and that Apathy specifically is a *terrible* choice for a Rank 1 Sin on a Path intended for players to use. See Missing Post for details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually interested in this, so I will wait until a mod unlocks it before commenting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563596#post1563596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI also think there's an IC problem where the philosophy of &quot;True Will&quot; remains somewhat vague and non-committal from a philosophical or ideological point of view, and I think that lack of firm convictions would leave it too weak to resist the degrading influence of the Beast. I think you need to commit more to a particular direction, in one of a few possible ways:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm less troubled if what attainment exactly means is somewhat diffuse; I don't think that is too important as long as the player has an idea what it means for their character. However, I think my biggest failure so far was to properly convey what the Path considers to be &quot;True Will&quot;, as opposed to other (and legitimate) interpretations. Since I've attempted that three or four times by now I'm a bit at loss and possibly at the limit of my abilities.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Do As Thou Wilt&quot; of this Path, <i>opposed</i> to that of the Road of Sin is that it requires harmonic integration of the Self in the universe. It says that if you neglect that aspect, you can not Do As Thou Wilt because it is a direct contradiction of Will. Conscience as a Virtue hinges on that, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T14:54:16-07:00","id":1563606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563600#post1563600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! I consider the conflict between Self, Beast, and Society to be the main difficulty you feel is missing, and in particular the the conflict between Rank 5 / 6 Sins. I don't see them as a direct contradiction though:<br /> <br /> &quot;Treat others as you would be treated&quot; comes directly from the Path of Self-Focus, which is <i>very</i> self-centered. The reason is that the moral judgement lies with the character, and not an external list of ethics. It also does not mean it is 'nice'; the flip-side and implicit result is &quot;eye for an eye&quot; when it comes to enforcement of those judgements.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I think it is impossible to make a list of Sins that is both playable and sufficiently nuanced, at least with my command of English. IMO &quot;Becoming blood bound&quot; should imply that loss of autonomy in general is considered a bad thing and something like authoritarian rules are at the very least suspect.<br /> <br /> But if that isn't the case, then the description and general Ethics do not cover enough of those nuances. I will have another look whether I can include some more specifics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using your Blood Bond point as an example, you're right that it clearly implies that losing autonomy is regarded negatively. But it's not a <b>Sin</b>; only the Blood Bond itself is listed as a Sin. So, my version of that Tenet would be something like &quot;Submitting to the Authority of Another,&quot; where it more generally covers any kind of surrender to hierarchy, the sublimation of the True Will. A Blood Bond <b>may</b> qualify, if the Regnant uses the power of the Bond to place the True Will follower in a subservient position. But it at least potentially leaves room for a mutual Blood Bond between lovers, with neither trying to assert power over the other. And it also adds an additional dimension of drama, because now a core Tenet of the Path is going to constantly put the Vampire in conflict with the local Prince, Archbishop, etc. It's more vague, but I still think it's conceptually clear enough that you're rarely going to end up in arguments over interpretation.<br /> <br /> The Path of Self-Focus was one I thought might also be a good model for the Path you're trying to create, but I haven't looked at it as closely as some of the others I've mentioned. The thing is, Self-Focus doesn't also have &quot;acting against your Self-Interest&quot; as a Sin in the same Hierarchy. The Path of Self-Focus is self-<b>absorbed</b>, but it's a Stoic/Quietist Path that actively preaches <b>against</b> trying to exert your Will over the wider world, hence &quot;Interfering with the Universe&quot; being among the listed Sins. This clashes heavily with the ideology/psychology of the Road of Sin, at least as I understand it.<br /> <br /> I do understand that &quot;Treat others as you would be treated&quot; isn't always nice, eye-for-an-eye and all that. But my point is that it fundamentally clashes with the precepts of the Road of Sin. The Road of Sin is &quot;It's All About Me.&quot; The Golden Rule is, in essence, &quot;It's Not All About Me.&quot; To quickly reference a point from my previous post, Egocentrism is a Feature of the Road of Sin, not a Bug, and I don't think it works well as an ideological foundation for a Path that is supposed to care about more than just the personal Desires of the Sinner. I don't think the Road of Sin <b>works</b> if the Vampire doesn't consider their own personal Desires to be the most important thing in their existence.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think the synthesis you're trying to achieve here is impossible, but I do think it'll be very challenging, and the arguments up to this point haven't resolved the contradiction for me. I'm not familiar enough with Crowley to know if his work helps to marry those two concepts better, but my limited understanding of his position has always been more &quot;Enlightened Egoist&quot; than &quot;We are all part of something greater, and need to find our place within that system.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think trying to use the Road of Sin as your baseline is actually the mistake here, not the concept itself. I think there are other Paths or Roads, like the Beast, that would serve as a better starting point for a Path that wants to balance the selfishness of the Vampire with an acknowledgement of a higher order that the Vampire has to align itself with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563600#post1563600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually interested in this, so I will wait until a mod unlocks it before commenting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had some thoughts about my initial take since then anyways, so I can elaborate a little more here.<br /> <br /> My initial argument was that &quot;Apathy&quot; is a trait that will rarely, if ever, be present in an active PC, at least during a play session. They are going to have goals, and they will be actively pursuing them. If a PC falls guilty of the Sin of &quot;Apathy,&quot; then it's because they chose to do so. There's no sense in which the story itself can force the PC into a position where they might fall from this Path despite the wishes of the player.<br /> <br /> I've softened my take a little bit, but I do still think there's a difficulty that has to do with why I think &quot;Apathy&quot; might be better for Rank 8, for example. My example for comparison is how Humanity has &quot;Selfish Thoughts&quot; as a Rank 10 Sin. The tricky thing about a &quot;thought-crime&quot; Sin is that it can be very open to the kinds of debates that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">monteparnas</a> was discussing earlier when you leave what qualifies as a Sin too vague or open to interpretation. Now, if that Sin is only going to keep the Character from reaching the highest Ranks of a Path, you can justify being a bit of a hard-ass about it as a Storyteller. But if &quot;Apathy&quot; is going to potentially <b>End A Character</b> by turning them into a Wight if they fail their Path roll, are you gonna want to initiate that without a Really Extreme and Unambiguous example of &quot;Apathy&quot; from the character? Are you going to risk removing a character from play because he decided to sit out some random social drama due to &quot;apathy&quot;? Or will you only call them on it when their Vampire is literally choosing to be neckbeard couch potato, which literally no PC is ever going to be?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563600#post1563600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm less troubled if what attainment exactly means is somewhat diffuse; I don't think that is too important as long as the player has an idea what it means for their character. However, I think my biggest failure so far was to properly convey what the Path considers to be &quot;True Will&quot;, as opposed to other (and legitimate) interpretations. Since I've attempted that three or four times by now I'm a bit at loss and possibly at the limit of my abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have an issue with the Path not having a singular vision of what True Will will look like after it's been developed. But I do have an issue with the fact that the Path as currently written doesn't seem to provide much direction for how to discover that True Will, either. You haven't given us a clear idea of what True Will <b>is</b> versus what it <b>isn't</b>. And I've already made my criticisms regarding why I think gesturing in the direction of the Road of Sin doesn't work for the specific Path that you are trying to put together here. I think the Path of Metamorphosis is a really good example of illustrating how you can have a Path that can lead off in many different directions, but still has enough of a coherent ideological concept that you can see how all those different destinations can be found along the same Path.<br /> <br /> And again, I find myself wondering if it really needs to be a <b>Path of Enlightenment</b>, a radical shift in the identity and ethics of the Vampire that results in an entirely new Hierarchy of Sins that the character needs to operate within, or should it just be a <b>philosophy</b> of self-actualization that a Vampire <b>or</b> Human could follow, while still feeling bound by the moral norms of Humanity?<br /> <br /> Again, referencing my hidden previous post, I don't think there's a single Path in (modern) Vampire that keeps Conscience <b>and</b> Self-Control. And while there were some Roads that did so, it's already been mentioned how the differences between the modern Paths and medieval Roads partly have to do with different themes and relations with society at large for the different settings. But also, the Roads that <b>did</b> allow you to keep Conscience and Self-Control were the ones most similar to modern Vampire's notion of Humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563600#post1563600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Do As Thou Wilt&quot; of this Path, <i>opposed</i> to that of the Road of Sin is that it requires harmonic integration of the Self in the universe. It says that if you neglect that aspect, you can not Do As Thou Wilt because it is a direct contradiction of Will. Conscience as a Virtue hinges on that, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, But Why?<br /> <br /> I think <b>this </b>is the part of the Path's philosophy that we're really missing that would help it all make sense. From the perspective of the Road of Sin, it's absolute nonsense. So where did this idea come from? Why exactly does &quot;True Will&quot; require this harmony between the Self and the Universe? It can't just be pragmatism, or we're back to Enlightened Egoism. So it seems like there has to be some kind of philosophical or spiritual principle explaining this ideological commitment, and I haven't been able to find it in what you've put forward so far.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T18:09:21-07:00","id":1563610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using your Blood Bond point as an example, you're right that it clearly implies that losing autonomy is regarded negatively. But it's not a <b>Sin</b>; only the Blood Bond itself is listed as a Sin. So, my version of that Tenet would be something like &quot;Submitting to the Authority of Another,&quot; where it more generally covers any kind of surrender to hierarchy, the sublimation of the True Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is if I do that, it is again inaccurate. Submission to authority would by itself be no issue as long as the authority does not impede the freedom of the practitioner (see the brief discussion with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> earlier). I took out the nuance to allow a stringent list with quantifiable game events to avoid those problems, re-introducing it would mean going back to much how the first version looked. Several of these nuances would also occupy spots on different Ranks of the Hierarchy even if they serve similar concepts; I think the better alternative is that the Path description is good enough to allow STs and player to know when to call for a roll, even if the committed Sin is not explicitly listed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Self-Focus is self-<b>absorbed</b>, but it's a Stoic/Quietist Path that actively preaches <b>against</b> trying to exert your Will over the wider world, hence &quot;Interfering with the Universe&quot; being among the listed Sins. This clashes heavily with the ideology/psychology of the Road of Sin, at least as I understand it.<br /> <br /> I do understand that &quot;Treat others as you would be treated&quot; isn't always nice, eye-for-an-eye and all that. But my point is that it fundamentally clashes with the precepts of the Road of Sin. The Road of Sin is &quot;It's All About Me.&quot; The Golden Rule is, in essence, &quot;It's Not All About Me.&quot; To quickly reference a point from my previous post, Egocentrism is a Feature of the Road of Sin, not a Bug, and I don't think it works well as an ideological foundation for a Path that is supposed to care about more than just the personal Desires of the Sinner. I don't think the Road of Sin <b>works</b> if the Vampire doesn't consider their own personal Desires to be the most important thing in their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just in case that my description on this was misleading: While the Path evolved from the Road of Sin, it's not a Path on the Road of Sin. It's meant to be a modern evolution created by someone who studied the Road and put their own spin on its philosophy.<br /> <br /> The description text is there because I stared with two Paths of the Road as a basis, and because I think a similar development could be likely from a Watsonian perspective. I don't think having a kindred study the Path and think &quot;Well, that would be more interesting with an actual integration into society&quot; is too far fetched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if &quot;Apathy&quot; is going to potentially <b>End A Character</b> by turning them into a Wight if they fail their Path roll, are you gonna want to initiate that without a Really Extreme and Unambiguous example of &quot;Apathy&quot; from the character? Are you going to risk removing a character from play because he decided to sit out some random social drama due to &quot;apathy&quot;? Or will you only call them on it when their Vampire is literally choosing to be neckbeard couch potato, which literally no PC is ever going to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The placement as the cardinal Sin is because the whole Path requires the presence of desire as the driving force behind everything else. The more nuanced description was &quot;If you have no more desires except for what your Beast or others tell you to do.&quot;<br /> As a gameplay state I recognize this is very unlikely to happen, but it can; vampires falling into deep depression or being deliberately put into this kind of state through the machinations of another isn't unheard of. It's basically the favorite pastime for Setites. Apathy seemed like an apt descriptor, but it's maybe too reductive. It could do with better phrasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have an issue with the Path not having a singular vision of what True Will will look like after it's been developed. But I do have an issue with the fact that the Path as currently written doesn't seem to provide much direction for how to discover that True Will, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with that; the really long post on Page 1 I made to address the individual Sins had the process still baked into them, so it got lost when I took that out to simplify them. I need to put that back into the Path description and Ethics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, I find myself wondering if it really needs to be a <b>Path of Enlightenment</b>, a radical shift in the identity and ethics of the Vampire that results in an entirely new Hierarchy of Sins that the character needs to operate within, or should it just be a <b>philosophy</b> of self-actualization that a Vampire <b>or</b> Human could follow, while still feeling bound by the moral norms of Humanity?<br /> <br /> Again, referencing my hidden previous post, I don't think there's a single Path in (modern) Vampire that keeps Conscience <b>and</b> Self-Control. And while there were some Roads that did so, it's already been mentioned how the differences between the modern Paths and medieval Roads partly have to do with different themes and relations with society at large for the different settings. But also, the Roads that <b>did</b> allow you to keep Conscience and Self-Control were the ones most similar to modern Vampire's notion of Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few that do, Path of Honorable Accord and Path of Redemption from the top of my mind. The question why not simply making it a philosophy on top of Humanity I answered earlier in the thread, but the main reason is because it offers an alternative to those who recognize that human ethics can not apply to them as vampires with a Beast any longer. That's basically every Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, But Why?<br /> <br /> I think <b>this </b>is the part of the Path's philosophy that we're really missing that would help it all make sense. From the perspective of the Road of Sin, it's absolute nonsense. So where did this idea come from? Why exactly does &quot;True Will&quot; require this harmony between the Self and the Universe? It can't just be pragmatism, or we're back to Enlightened Egoism. So it seems like there has to be some kind of philosophical or spiritual principle explaining this ideological commitment, and I haven't been able to find it in what you've put forward so far.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I wanted to make a Path the uses Conscience and Self-Control that combines a self-centered perspective with social elements that come up in gameplay. When I made the first draft I recognized how similar it was to the thelemic version of True Will, so I used that as a further template.<br /> <br /> The philosophic concept is more complicated and what I think I struggled with conveying so far. There's a wiki article on it that isn't really good, and the detailed explanation by Crowley is mostly in his Liber Al vel Legis if you are interested. It's the source of the &quot;Do what thou wilt&quot; quote, btw.<br /> But I will try to give the condensed reasoning:<br /> <br /> Do what you will is the law<br /> So, what is your will? To know your will, you need to know who you are and why you are.<br /> The Why is your purpose - your destiny - your place in the cosmic order.<br /> Desires by themselves are banal. Satisfying ego-driven, base desires can result in conflict with the world - i.e. they can disrupt harmony.<br /> Therefore, poorly conceived desires can not be your True Will; that would be a paradox.<br /> <br /> The whole resulting process of refining base desires into True Will was what I was trying to shove into the Sins in the first version, which resulted in this weird meta-Path construct - that wasn't even my attempt, more of a side effect.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T19:57:20-07:00","id":1563611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563610#post1563610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few that do, Path of Honorable Accord and Path of Redemption from the top of my mind. The question why not simply making it a philosophy on top of Humanity I answered earlier in the thread, but the main reason is because it offers an alternative to those who recognize that human ethics can not apply to them as vampires with a Beast any longer. That's basically every Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to concede that I forgot about the Path of Redemption, and I genuinely thought Honourable Accord used Conviction. My bad.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, best of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T22:47:16-07:00","id":1563614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563606#post1563606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can't just be pragmatism, or we're back to Enlightened Egoism. So it seems like there has to be some kind of philosophical or spiritual principle explaining this ideological commitment, and I haven't been able to find it in what you've put forward so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, that's where understanding Thelema really helps getting this Path.<br /> <br /> Long story short, Crowley's True Will is actually the opposite of Enlightened Egoism. For him, a will based solely on the self is too limited and ignorant, it is just self-deception.<br /> <br /> True Will would be what surfaces when you actually understand the world, your place in it and what reality you want to live in. Refusing to follow tradition in favor of direct satisfaction is as much blind slavery as denying satisfaction in favor of tradition for its own sake.<br /> <br /> Rather, you must understand why the tradition exists, why you feel satisfaction with things, and what both will lead to in the long run. When you manage to look past assumptions and see how everything connects, you become able to chose the person you <i><b>want</b></i> to be and the world you <i><b>want</b></i> to help build. This is True Will.<br /> <br /> While this Path isn't perfectly Crowleyan, this is more or less the key point: True Will isn't here a measure of direct satisfaction, it's commitment to a goal you built yourself being mindful of the consequences, because a consequence you don't want is a failure of Will.<br /> <br /> Crowley recognizes we are social by nature. A goal that ignores the community isn't serving your Will because it's ignoring that you care by your own nature and is a part of it as a fact of reality. This Path does something similar by acknowledging you live in society and needs it, so your True Will must fit: if your actions make society reject you, or degrade it into a society you don't want to live in, they were not actions of Will, but of stupidity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T23:01:08-07:00","id":1563616,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> <br /> Based on that, I can see where my lack of understanding of the influential sources is impairing my ability to understand the philosophical foundations, and those are probably more coherent than I've given them credit for.<br /> <br /> I still think the mechanics are <b>REALLY</b> bad. And I dunno if I have the energy/spoons to address my concerns currently, beyond what I've already said. I genuinely don't think that the Humanity system is even worth bothering to include with a Hierarchy of Sins that is so easy to follow, at least when you only care about staying in that &quot;comfort zone&quot; of Rank 5-7. Maybe that's another mistake on my part, but this Parh just feels way too damn Easy Mode to me. It is unsatisfying from the OOC perspective of drama and tension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  I wrote this way too late and tagged a person that doesn't exist. Stupid Warcraft putting the term 'Voidwalker' into my brain. 08-30-2026, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T23:06:40-07:00","id":1563617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563610#post1563610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that is if I do that, it is again inaccurate. Submission to authority would by itself be no issue as long as the authority does not impede the freedom of the practitioner (see the brief discussion with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> earlier).</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Alright, I'll take the job. But not because you told me to.&quot;</i> - average Path follower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T23:53:25-07:00","id":1563621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563616#post1563616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24256-voidwalker\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24256\" data-vbnamecard=\"24256\">Voidwalker</a><br /> <br /> Based on that, I can see where my lack of understanding of the influential sources is impairing my ability to understand the philosophical foundations, and those are probably more coherent than I've given them credit for.<br /> <br /> I still think the mechanics are <b>REALLY</b> bad. And I dunno if I have the energy/spoons to address my concerns currently, beyond what I've already said. I genuinely don't think that the Humanity system is even worth bothering to include with a Hierarchy of Sins that is so easy to follow, at least when you only care about staying in that &quot;comfort zone&quot; of Rank 5-7. Maybe that's another mistake on my part, but this Parh just feels way too damn Easy Mode to me. It is unsatisfying from the OOC perspective of drama and tension.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said earlier a good framework to compare was Eastern Paradox. Basically my impression is that this Path requires the player to define what their True Will is, in a similar way to how Eastern Paradox requires you to define your Svadharma.<br /> <br /> I got the impression the most recent iteration addressed it, but already understanding the foundations may be what's making it click for me more readily. In this sense your observation is invaluable as a measure of how well the Path is explaining itself.<br /> <br /> Basically, a lot of its teeth should come from a defined Will, because within this framework the Will is a more holistic, stable construct than just &quot;whatever I want now&quot;. Picture the player talking with the ST about their long term goals and strategies, and everything in the Path will then be measured against this. You can surely change opinion later, but not in the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T00:29:39-07:00","id":1563623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563621#post1563621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said earlier a good framework to compare was Eastern Paradox. Basically my impression is that this Path requires the player to define what their True Will is, in a similar way to how Eastern Paradox requires you to define your Svadharma.<br /> <br /> I got the impression the most recent iteration addressed it, but already understanding the foundations may be what's making it click for me more readily. In this sense your observation is invaluable as a measure of how well the Path is explaining itself.<br /> <br /> Basically, a lot of its teeth should come from a defined Will, because within this framework the Will is a more holistic, stable construct than just &quot;whatever I want now&quot;. Picture the player talking with the ST about their long term goals and strategies, and everything in the Path will then be measured against this. You can surely change opinion later, but not in the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked your reference to the Path of Paradox, for sure. But I almost feel like the old Hierarchy of Sins made more sense if the character's personal concept of &quot;True Will&quot; itself is where we're supposed to find the &quot;teeth.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't Frenzy.<br /> <br /> Don't get forced into a Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> Don't be &quot;Apathetic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know if I can conceive of a more Platonic Ideal of &quot;The Path of What I Wanted to Do Anyways&quot; than what this sounds like to me.<br /> <br /> This was why I earlier mentioned how I understood the choices around each Sin <b>individually</b>, but <b>collectively</b> I think they add up to a nightmare regardless.<br /> <br /> <b>I don't care</b> if these are consistent with the principles of Thelema.<br /> <br /> They're <b>Easy.</b><br /> <br /> They're <b>Boring.</b><br /> <br /> They're <b>Flavourless.</b><br /> <br /> If you can't make a Thelema-flavoured Path that is actually capable of challenging a follower, then don't make a Path. Unless you presume that the mortal Crowley was on a Path of Enlightenment, the ideas alone do not justify a radically and fundamentally different moral standard, in the form of an alternative Hierarchy of Sins.<br /> <br /> That was a lot of why I was ready to just call it and duck out. When Voidshaper* mentioned how a lot of my points would entail going backwards to the older Hierarchy that everyone was criticizing, the whole thing started to feel like a mess that would only get messier if I kept pushing my own subjective take.<br /> <br /> I don't think this adds up to something that should qualify as a Path of Enlightenment, as I have seen it formulated so far.<br /> <br /> Part of that probably comes from my tendency to view Paths as entailing some degree of fanaticism that this concept seems to lack.<br /> <br /> But we can point to moments in this specific thread where I was talking a lot of shit, so I don't want to pretend that me being unpersuaded is a damning indictment. If people feel that my insights add something of value, I'll keep sharing them. But I don't want to just be a contrarian dick and a buzzkill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  * Oops I did it again v_v 08-30-2026, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T01:44:45-07:00","id":1563626,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> It's perfectly valid criticism, I specifically asked for feedback on whether the Path would be attractive for a player. And in case I messed that up too: I value your comments on it and find them useful - my replies are as much for myself as they are for you, the explanations help me to verify or invalidate my decisions. The spoons are yours to give or not, of course.<br /> <br /> If anything this thread demonstrates my infuriating habit of forgetting that people can not look into my head and follow my reasoning if I don't write it down, something I have been trying to work on - still needs work, as it stands. That's also why I value the community feedback so much, because it helps me to better present ideas to my players.<br /> <br /> The Sins are currently very much reduced from their original intent, and I agree that took out too much of the friction. I still think any adjustments to the Hierarchy should be careful enough to not lose the stringency, and the bulk of revision should go into description and Ethics to amend them. But it's fine to change them for the better.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I may have to directly quote your explanation of True Will, if that is ok with you. It's a lot more coherent than what I have been able to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T03:04:49-07:00","id":1563627,"title":"","content":"You're welcome, happy I could help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T08:44:47-07:00","id":1563635,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> I never got the sense that you were frustrated or uninterested in my criticisms. I was just getting frustrated because it felt like we were talking past each other, and I didn't want to be an ass about it.<br /> <br /> Thanks again <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> for an excellent explanation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I definitely appreciate what this Path is trying to do. It feels like there's a lack of a suitable Road or Path for, for example, esoterically-minded Tremere elders. Most of the other more mystical Paths are more specialized and rarely found outside specific groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T11:34:05-07:00","id":1563638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563626#post1563626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> It's perfectly valid criticism, I specifically asked for feedback on whether the Path would be attractive for a player.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still feels a bit vague for me to play it out. 'I do what I want', 'the path of the Chaotic Neutral', 'It's what my character would do'. The 'let's partaaaaay path, but not really'.<br /> <br /> The useful part of paths to me are a clear identity or clear conflict.<br /> <br /> Easy to understand path examples:<br /> <br /> Path of the Feral Heart: <i>&quot;You get to be an animal man. You get to be wolverine. You get to live with like your instinct.&quot;</i><br /> Path of Honorable Accord: <i>&quot;You wanna be like a knight, but a screwed up undead vampire knight? Like undead nobility. Super diligent to your honor and honesty except you're still a monster&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Both of them have very clear archetypes they fulfil.<br /> <br /> Path of the Feral Heart<i>: &quot;You gotta live outside civilization, modernity is in complete unbalance. Cities are overgrown hives man, modern tech is poison. You gotta let all that stuff go, if you can't you gotta let as much of it go as possible&quot;</i><br /> Path of Honorable Accord<i> &quot;Honor isn't optional for you, it's what keeps you together. Your word isn't just your bond man, it's like your soul.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Both of them have very clear conflicts.<br /> <br /> Path of the True Will: <i>&quot;Are you an ascetic, a wannabe philosopher king, a party animal, a wannabe navel-gazing philosopher (don't knock this, this is a good archetype even if I word it as a negative), a sensationalist? I don't know.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Path of the True Will: <i>&quot;Current sins are mostly just hedonism except don't overdo it and be polite so... not much conflict? If I define my own motivation as my True Will it's just entirely context dependent on my character and the path is sort of unnecessary. Since I don't have a clear archetype for the path I don't have a clear conflict either? Do I need the st to tailor make some path related stuff like friction with groups that aren't my fellow pcs? Because that's not going to happen nine times out of ten. I don't get how this comes up in play.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T13:50:38-07:00","id":1563642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563638#post1563638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The useful part of paths to me are a clear identity or clear conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your preference for archetypical Paths is noted, but I'm afraid I can't accommodate for it. Like with other Paths based around faith or philosophy (Metamorphosis, Entelechy, Self-Focus, etc), adding an archetype would defeat the purpose. They are meant to support an identity, but don't prescribe one.<br /> <br /> I'm working on adding more engaging conflict, but I need to wear my thinking cap for a bit to properly mill over on how to implement the changes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-30-2026, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T17:07:09-07:00","id":1563652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563638#post1563638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still feels a bit vague for me to play it out. 'I do what I want', 'the path of the Chaotic Neutral', 'It's what my character would do'. The 'let's partaaaaay path, but not really'.<br /> <br /> The useful part of paths to me are a clear identity or clear conflict.<br /> <br /> Easy to understand path examples:<br /> <br /> Path of the Feral Heart: <i>&quot;You get to be an animal man. You get to be wolverine. You get to live with like your instinct.&quot;</i><br /> Path of Honorable Accord: <i>&quot;You wanna be like a knight, but a screwed up undead vampire knight? Like undead nobility. Super diligent to your honor and honesty except you're still a monster&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Both of them have very clear archetypes they fulfil.<br /> <br /> Path of the Feral Heart<i>: &quot;You gotta live outside civilization, modernity is in complete unbalance. Cities are overgrown hives man, modern tech is poison. You gotta let all that stuff go, if you can't you gotta let as much of it go as possible&quot;</i><br /> Path of Honorable Accord<i> &quot;Honor isn't optional for you, it's what keeps you together. Your word isn't just your bond man, it's like your soul.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Both of them have very clear conflicts.<br /> <br /> Path of the True Will: <i>&quot;Are you an ascetic, a wannabe philosopher king, a party animal, a wannabe navel-gazing philosopher (don't knock this, this is a good archetype even if I word it as a negative), a sensationalist? I don't know.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Path of the True Will: <i>&quot;Current sins are mostly just hedonism except don't overdo it and be polite so... not much conflict? If I define my own motivation as my True Will it's just entirely context dependent on my character and the path is sort of unnecessary. Since I don't have a clear archetype for the path I don't have a clear conflict either? Do I need the st to tailor make some path related stuff like friction with groups that aren't my fellow pcs? Because that's not going to happen nine times out of ten. I don't get how this comes up in play.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with what you've said about the dramatic utility of a Path being in its ability to add conflict or controversy to the story, hence many of my criticisms. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> has already mentioned, there are plenty of Paths that aren't aimed at a specific &quot;role.&quot; It's why I've often used the term &quot;Mission&quot; in my posts, but you could also use things like &quot;Code&quot; or &quot;Principle(s).&quot; Metamorphosis is, again, a prime example of a Path where the destination is somewhat vague, and could vary depending on each traveler of the Path. But it has enough structure and conceptual coherence that you can understand how everyone is still following the same Path.<br /> <br /> Even if the ultimate goal of Metamorphosis is somewhat fluid, there are a few defining features of &quot;Azhi Dahaka&quot; that help establish the direction that the Path is aimed. But not every Path is aimed at a particular role or outcome, they are just alternative normative frameworks for one's continued existence as a Vampire. But if the Path doesn't have a clear destination, I do think that the boundaries of the Path, in the form of its Hierarchy of Sins, become more important in establishing what it means to follow the Path.<br /> <br /> Going back, I notice how in the intro post you mention that this isn't supposed to be an explicit commentary on or reference to Thelema. But if you don't want to directly reference Thelema, you may still want to use it to help get an idea of what philosophies and spiritual beliefs would lead someone to adopt a Thelema-like conception of &quot;True Will.&quot;<br /> <br /> To go back to one of those places where it felt like we weren't connecting before, I didn't keep bringing up the Road of Sin because I thought you were trying to make a new Path for that Road. I brought it up because you describe the Road of Sin as where the Path of the True Will &quot;traces back to,&quot; like it's a philosophical ancestor. But based on my understanding of the Road of Sin, the relationship between it and the Path of True Will that you describe seems almost analogous to the relationship between Christianity and Satanism, where the latter is almost an antithesis of the former rather than a direct intellectual descendant.<br /> <br /> Part of why I'm so invested in this topic is because I'm a fan of the Via Adversarius, btw <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So some of what I think is missing is the explanation of What Happened in the middle: what other ideas led someone to take the Road of Sin in such a radically different direction? And, again, even if you don't want this to specifically be a Path of Thelema, the same ideas that influenced Crowley and the direction that Thelema went may help you find answers for those questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T18:12:33-07:00","id":1563658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563652#post1563652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely agree with what you've said about the dramatic utility of a Path being in its ability to add conflict or controversy to the story, hence many of my criticisms. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> has already mentioned, there are plenty of Paths that aren't aimed at a specific &quot;role.&quot; It's why I've often used the term &quot;Mission&quot; in my posts, but you could also use things like &quot;Code&quot; or &quot;Principle(s).&quot; Metamorphosis is, again, a prime example of a Path where the destination is somewhat vague, and could vary depending on each traveler of the Path. But it has enough structure and conceptual coherence that you can understand how everyone is still following the same Path.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Path of Metamorphosis has a good identity. 'undead transhumanist with a dash or more of body horror'. It's quite strong a concept. The description of the path emphasize what kind of person a metamorphist is quite strongly. It has both a clear identity and a clear conflict bundled into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T18:16:55-07:00","id":1563659,"title":"","content":"One thing that occurred to me is that one natural conflict of this kind of philosophy is having to go back to the drawing board from time to time.<br /> <br /> You study reality, reach conclusions, develop a framework to achieve your goals... And after all that finds out you miscalculated a lot of stuff. You're faced with unexpected choices, results of your actions don't follow predictions, the role you want to fulfill don't work as planned and your goals are being hindered or revealed to not be what you expected.<br /> <br /> If True Will is defined both in terms of what you want to become and how you think it will play out, we add a failure state that don't need to be a sin directly, but creates a requirement to think about your experiences, revise what True Will means to you and decide how to deal with past failures, and how you go about that may have sins attached.<br /> <br /> Even Apathy can maybe be exchanged for Avoid Evaluation, where the process of revising your True Will, which should not be simple or fast, is also a fundamental piece of the Path. It has higher levels measuring your ability to stay true to your True Will, while the basic level asks if you're still putting the effort to <i>define</i> it, to know what your True Will is, which is a different failure state.<br /> <br /> With that the evolution of the hierarchy will be: define what you Want -&gt; decide how to Get it -&gt; follow the Plan -&gt; do so Competently -&gt; get the Result. To regret your choices is to fail at the last stretch, but to just go with the flow is to fail at the second or third steps, which is way more serious. And the Worse Sin isn't Apathy in the regular sense, but in the specific definition of the Path: refusal to take it seriously.<br /> <br /> As a side note, a Hedonism Path based on the actual teachings of Epicurus would also be an interesting thing to try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T18:36:09-07:00","id":1563660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563658#post1563658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Metamorphosis has a good identity. 'undead transhumanist with a dash or more of body horror'. It's quite strong a concept. The description of the path emphasize what kind of person a metamorphist is quite strongly. It has both a clear identity and a clear conflict bundled into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It most definitely has not.<br /> <br /> Metamorphosis has a presentation that deliver well an image, but the actual ethics and sins are by design not clear in identity or conflict.<br /> <br /> The Path is built for you to decide what a final transcence looks like for your character and to not be the same thing for every follower. And identity and conflict are completely dependent on what you decide transcendence means for you.<br /> <br /> What happens is that it validates and reference repeatedly the most basic Tzimisce stereotype, which gives you a ready to use example of how the Path can look like. That can easily look like being clear, but it's not. Read the actual ethics and sins and you have a framework where this example is actually only a small set of possible legitimate manifestations.<br /> <br /> Really the only common line between followers is that seeking transcendence should be more important than anything else, it's the &quot;be ready to sacrifice anything for it&quot; attitude. Everything else is just optional window dressing and you are given but one example of how to dress your window.<br /> <br /> Not saying it doesn't work as a Path. It surely do. But it's not a clear archetype, and if you find it easy to understand I think there's a non trivial chance that you didn't actually understood it.<br /> <br /> Although it is a good example of presentation that may serve here. One thing this Path here may need is an example that serves as that archetypal anchor to give a starting point and easy to use example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T19:23:48-07:00","id":1563662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563658#post1563658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Metamorphosis has a good identity. 'undead transhumanist with a dash or more of body horror'. It's quite strong a concept. The description of the path emphasize what kind of person a metamorphist is quite strongly. It has both a clear identity and a clear conflict bundled into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Transhumanism&quot; (or &quot;Transvampirism&quot; in this case?) is an important concept, for sure, but that is a pretty broad topic. But &quot;body horror&quot; is absolutely not a necessity. The medieval Via Mutationis notably recognized the Path of Spirit as equally valid to the Path of Flesh, and while most modern-day Metamorphosists tend to focus on physical transformation, &quot;body horror&quot; really doesn't need to come into it. I can't find a clear reference quickly to be sure of the name, but the Path of Metamorphosis would also include Tzimisce who abstain from vitae as much as possible in the hopes of transcending their dependence upon it, I believe they're referred to as &quot;Exsanguinists.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd actually say that &quot;vampire supremacy&quot; is probably more intrinsic to the Path of Metamorphosis than &quot;body horror.&quot; But the body horror stuff was prominently associated with the Clan early on, and tended to be edgy and meant to shock, so it stood out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T00:36:25-07:00","id":1563674,"title":"","content":"I think what may be happening is that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28924\" data-vbnamecard=\"28924\">Tjalei</a> has a broader understanding of what an archetype for a Path is; taking Entelechy as an example, the bearing is 'Stoic'. I don't consider that by itself an identity, but that may be too narrow. My guess is that something like 'Stoic' or 'Transhumanist' evokes a clear picture because they are familiar concepts, whereas the Path of Desire and True Will can not do that because I conjured it up.<br /> <br /> Which brings me back to reworking the Path description and Ethics, because that is where I need to do that. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> Describing some of the historic IC development is a good idea, I can basically wrap this thread into a story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I'm currently floating 'self-deception' as a possible replacement for Apathy. Path of the Eightfold Wheel codifies that as &quot;Failure to seek self-knowledge&quot;, which would tie in with the reflection and refinement of the self you mention. I'm just not sure whether this is any less abstract as a Sin.<br /> <br /> An Epicurean Path would be fun. We already have stoics for some good conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T01:46:53-07:00","id":1563676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563674#post1563674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what may be happening is that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28924\" data-vbnamecard=\"28924\">Tjalei</a> has a broader understanding of what an archetype for a Path is; taking Entelechy as an example, the bearing is 'Stoic'. I don't consider that by itself an identity, but that may be too narrow. My guess is that something like 'Stoic' or 'Transhumanist' evokes a clear picture because they are familiar concepts, whereas the Path of Desire and True Will can not do that because I conjured it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah pretty much. A frame isn't vague even if the painting is a blank canvas <br /> <br /> There's also a focus on actual gameplay. <i>Vampire supremacist</i> may be accurate as words go, but if you tell that to a player they will image it as <i>vampire skinhead.</i><br /> If I open with <i>monstrous transhumanist with a dash of body horror</i> it's trivial to follow up with <i>they believe in an evolutionary chain, kine above animals, kindred above kine.</i> And also of course: <i>you don't have to go into body horror if you think it is gross</i>. It's practical. Depth can be added over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T07:42:54-07:00","id":1563686,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28924\" data-vbnamecard=\"28924\">Tjalei</a> I still have some issues with what you're saying, but I don't want to derail the thread, so if you want to keep discussing it we can maybe move to PMs or a new thread, unless <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> feels that exploring this tangent may have some utility for their project. The only thing I do want to say is that body horror being &quot;gross&quot; is absolutely not the issue here.<br /> <br /> I do think that the point about &quot;Bearing&quot; is a good one. It's not something I've given a lot of thought to, but you're right that having an idea of a common Bearing might help get across a more general sense of the &quot;identity&quot; of the Path. A few examples that might work would be &quot;Deliberate,&quot; &quot;Intentional,&quot; or &quot;Calculating,&quot; though I'm not entirely sure how those might function mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 08-31-2026, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T11:09:56-07:00","id":1563704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> Go ahead, I don't mind tangents. It's not a proper forum thread without a parallel discussion by page 3 anyway. <hr /><br /> Before I go over the description, I wanted to adjust the Hierarchy. Current outline:<br /> <br /> - Changed Rank 1 Sin to one for reflection and re-evaluation. This one needs to be properly explained in the description.<br /> - Rank 3 &quot;Becoming blood bound&quot; was broadened to allow for more triggers<br /> - Rank 4 &quot;Succumbing to Frenzy&quot; was broadened and moved to Rank 6, added social friction. Would like a snappier phrasing, but can't think of anything.<br /> - Bumped up severity of Rank 5 &amp; 6 to Rank 4 &amp; 5 respectively<br /> - Sins 7 &amp; 8 were very close, changed Rank 7 to something with more internal friction<br /> <br /> 1. Failure to seek self-knowledge<br /> 2. Losing Will or Virtue<br /> 3. Yielding a personal freedom<br /> 4. Acting against your own self interests<br /> 5. Failure to treat others as you would be treated<br /> 6. Putting desires of your Beast or another before your own<br /> 7. Forfeiting long-term for short-term progress<br /> 8. Refusing indulgence that harms none<br /> 9. Failing to explore a new desire<br /> 10. Feeling guilt for your actions<br /> <br /> In general, broader phrasing allows more for triggers but sacrifices unambiguity. I hope the altered phrasing is still quantifiable enough in gameplay. Let me know what you think, and also if it's enough added teeth. Personally I'm pretty happy with it, but don't let that stop you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:30:27-07:00","id":1563717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563676#post1563676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Vampire supremacist</i> may be accurate as words go, but if you tell that to a player they will image it as <i>vampire skinhead.</i><br /> If I open with <i>monstrous transhumanist with a dash of body horror</i> it's trivial to follow up with <i>they believe in an evolutionary chain, kine above animals, kindred above kine.</i> And also of course: <i>you don't have to go into body horror if you think it is gross</i>. It's practical. Depth can be added over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, based on what you're saying here, it sounds like you aren't talking about Paths needing to fit into a &quot;role.&quot; That sound more like a <b>Stereotype</b>.<br /> <br /> And your own response already demonstrates some of the limitations of that approach. Your &quot;stereotype&quot; for a (white) supremacist is a Skinhead, but the Ku Klux Klan would probably qualify just as well, and there are plenty of distinctions you can make between the two. There isn't any reason to prefer one interpretation over the other, which limits the utility of the expression unless you consider both options equally valid.<br /> <br /> Your use of the term &quot;transhumanist&quot; actually carries a similar issue, even if I do agree that it's appropriate. In my experience, the expression &quot;transhumanism&quot; tends to be associated more with a scientific/tech-oriented approach to things, folks turning themselves into cyborgs or uploading their consciousness. But Metamorphosis is as much a mystical and spiritual pursuit as it is a scientific one. Your use of the term &quot;transhumanist&quot; isn't necessarily any clearer than my use of the term &quot;vampire supremacy.&quot;<br /> <br /> But more importantly, the fact that &quot;skinhead&quot; is the first thing that pops into your head when I say &quot;vampire supremacy&quot; is completely irrelevant, because I am not talking about a Stereotype of the Path; I am talking about the actual philosophy of the Path of Metamorphosis, and I can clearly point to tenets of its ideology and actual mechanics like the use of Instinct as a Virtue to demonstrate my point. Your first impression just doesn't matter in the face of actual facts, and it demonstrates the limitations of trying to force a complex Path to fit into a neat little Stereotype you can sum up in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> You point out that there's no reason you can't elaborate and broaden the concept beyond the initial Stereotype, but then why do you <b>need</b> the Stereotype if it isn't going to cover everything anyways? I don't necessarily think it's bad if you <b>can</b> do it, but I think it's a mistake to treat it as a necessary component of a coherent Path. There are some Paths, like Metamorphosis, where it's probably a good thing if you can't come up with a neat little box that the majority of the Path followers can easily be lumped into, because diversity and individuality are the point.<br /> <br /> You might argue that you can defend your use of &quot;body horror&quot; in the same way, but I would disagree. However, it depends on a bit of clarification: when you say &quot;body<b> horror,</b>&quot; are you treating that as synonymous with &quot;body <b>modification</b>&quot;? I would treat those as distinct, but not entirely unrelated, concepts.<br /> <br /> For example, a Metamorphosist who uses Vicissitude to move their heart to a different part of their body as a defence against being staked is definitely engaging in body modification. But while it might be disgusting to watch, I don't think most folks would consider what amounts to a surgical procedure to be a form of body horror.<br /> <br /> For more of a grey area, if the Metamorphosist instead opted to strengthen their ribcage by reinforcing it with other rib bones (using the 6-dot power that lets you graft on other peoples' body parts), then that would probably count as body horror from the perspective of the person who probably has to be kept alive while their ribs are pulled out and moulded onto the Tzimisce's chest, while still also being body modification. And the appearance of the Tzimisce after the process may not be particularly &quot;horrifying.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, of course, a Tzimisce who turns themself into a writhing-mass of lamprey-like tentacles has probably crossed over properly into something you could call body horror.<br /> <br /> Now, usual caveats around personal taste, do what you want at your table, etc., part of why I'm pushing back against your Stereotype of Metamorphosis-as-body-horror is because, in my opinion, that is the Absolute Worst element of the Path of Metamorphosis and how it has sometimes been portrayed. Again, not because it's &quot;gross.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's because it's stupid.<br /> <br /> The idea of Tzimisce/Metamorphosists going out of their way to make themselves look monstrous as some kind of rejection of their humanity is childish edge-lord nonsense. They're still letting themselves be defined by humanity through their opposition to it. At best, it makes sense as a silly phase that Tzimisce neonates go through before they &quot;grow up&quot; and get serious about Metamorphosis. A better example of what a &quot;mature&quot; Metamorphosist might sound like would be Alucard telling Walter &quot;the trappings of mortal form are meaningless to me.&quot; Another good example is how Yorak's &quot;default&quot; appearance was that of an old man, despite Yorak being basically the Paragon of Metamorphosis in their night.<br /> <br /> A mature Metamorphosist would not let themselves get hung up on &quot;looking like a monster.&quot; They would coldly and rationally consider what form will best enable them to pursue their own ideal form of vampirism. A Metamorphosist who makes themself look monstrous because they think making their prey afraid will help them hunt is just as valid as a Metamorphosist who makes themself look as blandly human as possible as a form of camouflage for the hunt. What matters is that they are motivated by their desire to become a Perfect Being, not by their desire to give the concept of humanity the middle finger.<br /> <br /> In the words of Hannibal Lecter, &quot;No, [body horror] is coincidental!&quot;<br /> <br /> And, again, while taste and such are subjective, there are clear signs that some of the writers have come around to this way of thinking. Even by the time of Revised, you had various factions and ideologies among the Tzimisce that rejected the &quot;body horror&quot; concept, with groups like the Old Clan and the Children of the Dracon. But it's even more prominent in V20, with the Tzimisce write-up in (IIRC) <u>Lore of the Clans</u> basically being a discussion of how the obsession with monstrosity could be a sign of Kupala's corrupting influence. You can see a similar attitude in the discussion between Beckett and Vykos in BJD regarding the latter's decision to mutilate themself just to make a rhetorical point. Entertainingly edgy, sure, but still childish and stupid, for reasons that can easily be spelled out (pun intended).<br /> <br /> Again, if you can manage to sum all that up into a tidy little Stereotype you can easily share with someone, great. But I'm not shedding any tears if you can't. And I (playfully) think it's downright disrespectful to try and force the Path of Metamorphosis into the Worst Possible Stereotype you can imagine for it.<br /> <br /> (P.S. I've talked a lot about Stereotypes, and that term tends to be treated as inherently negative or pejorative. To be clear, I'm trying to use it in a neutral manner here, just as a description of what you seem to be talking about. Stereotypes are a kind of heuristic, and heuristics are useful. But they have limits, and you need to be careful of them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:46:34-07:00","id":1563719,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> While the seeking self-knowledge part is important, having &quot;Self-deception&quot; as the Rank 1 Sin may make it a bit easier to qualify what counts as a transgression. &quot;The True Will must Know Itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> The act of pursuing self-knowledge may work better at Rank 2, analogous to &quot;Neglecting to alter one's body&quot; on the Path of Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> While it needs to be defined more, I think it might be a good idea to replace &quot;self-interest&quot; with &quot;True Will&quot; in the Rank 4 Sin, just because of the common connotations of &quot;self-interest&quot; maybe obscuring the intended meaning a bit. While I understand it's inclusion better, I worry that &quot;Treat others as you wish to be treated&quot; might similarly carry too much conceptual baggage. Even if they stay as placeholders, those particular concepts could maybe be rephrased to connect them better with the elaboration you'll eventually be providing on the deeper philosophies.<br /> <br /> One idea I had for a &quot;custom&quot; Sin that might be appropriate to the Path is &quot;Thoughtless destruction.&quot; It leaves a lot of room for calculated violence, but condemns reckless and impulsive aggression, along with excessive collateral damage. I'd probably slot that into the Rank 4-6 range somewhere, but it's just an idea for you to consider. Similarly, &quot;Acting on impulse&quot; could work well as an option for the higher Ranks, could replace the altered Frenzy Sin, especially if you consider Frenzy as an &quot;impulse,&quot; but I think it may also cover the short-vs-long-term stuff you have at Rank 7 a bit more succinctly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do like &quot;Yielding personal freedom,&quot; it does a good job of covering a lot of ground while still being well-defined and consistent with the spirit of the Path. And Rank 3 is a nice and dramatically-appropriate place to put it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Split my post to hopefully avoid the wrath of the spam-filter x_x)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:21:59-07:00","id":1563722,"title":"","content":"The wrath of the spam filter is a fierce and terrifying one indeed.<br /> <br /> My own Metamorphosists usually skew Vicissitude entirely when working on themselves. I like the idea of the experience of the surgery being seen as part of the process.<br /> <br /> By fleshcrafting others you learn the physical workings of the body. But to truly transcend you have to feel the process with all attention you can give it, letting others excute your design while you focus on your senses.<br /> <br /> And I have been thinking for a time on doing a &quot;classic&quot; transhumanist with a techgnostic approach. Maybe even skewing Vicissitude altogether in the build to focus on the other two and Koldunic Sorcery (I like the Old Clan conceptually, but really not Dominate for the Tzimisce).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:32:16-07:00","id":1563724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563722#post1563722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own Metamorphosists usually skew Vicissitude entirely when working on themselves. I like the idea of the experience of the surgery being seen as part of the process.<br /> <br /> By fleshcrafting others you learn the physical workings of the body. But to truly transcend you have to feel the process with all attention you can give it, letting others excute your design while you focus on your senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I <b>like</b> that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Definitely an interesting angle!<br /> <br /> It also brings up a point I forgot in my previous text-wall, which is that you can justify a lot of body horror stuff as &quot;honing your craft.&quot; But it's still coincidental, a means rather than an end.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563722#post1563722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I have been thinking for a time on doing a &quot;classic&quot; transhumanist with a techgnostic approach. Maybe even skewing Vicissitude altogether in the build to focus on the other two and Koldunic Sorcery (I like the Old Clan conceptually, but really not Dominate for the Tzimisce).</div> </div> </div> </div>I myself am extremely fond of Koldunism as a component of Metamorphosis practice. A more techgnostic Tzimisce is also an interesting idea, though Thaumaturgy may be a bit more suited to that approach than Koldunic Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Oh, instead of turning themself into a disease like Demdemeh, they could turn themselves into a <b>computer virus</b>.<br /> <br /> I can see where Dominate Tzimisce kind of clash with the idea of the Clan leaning on rule-by-fear. But I also dig the classic &quot;Dracula&quot; Vampire approach it helps to accommodate (while Vlad himself, ironically, was part of the main Clan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:42:50-07:00","id":1563727,"title":"","content":"While my current Tzimisce isn't on Metamorphosis, she's a Pirate Party supporter with a plan for the ultimate Free Server, and once the time comes I want to explore some ideas for Vicissitude-imbued computers. One of them is to turn the biosphere itself into a Cloud Server through a fleshcrafting virus I'd make combining Vicissitude, Animalism and Blood Sorcery (as it is V5) to turn parts of the victim into a biological computing unity that network through the Elements.<br /> <br /> I think the idea that Dracula the Character and Dracula the Voivode would be from different Bloodlines fits well. And I definitely think the Voivode vibes more with Regular than Old Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar"