cessarily any clearer than my use of the term &quot;vampire supremacy.&quot;<br /> <br /> But more importantly, the fact that &quot;skinhead&quot; is the first thing that pops into your head when I say &quot;vampire supremacy&quot; is completely irrelevant, because I am not talking about a Stereotype of the Path; I am talking about the actual philosophy of the Path of Metamorphosis, and I can clearly point to tenets of its ideology and actual mechanics like the use of Instinct as a Virtue to demonstrate my point. Your first impression just doesn't matter in the face of actual facts, and it demonstrates the limitations of trying to force a complex Path to fit into a neat little Stereotype you can sum up in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> You point out that there's no reason you can't elaborate and broaden the concept beyond the initial Stereotype, but then why do you <b>need</b> the Stereotype if it isn't going to cover everything anyways? I don't necessarily think it's bad if you <b>can</b> do it, but I think it's a mistake to treat it as a necessary component of a coherent Path. There are some Paths, like Metamorphosis, where it's probably a good thing if you can't come up with a neat little box that the majority of the Path followers can easily be lumped into, because diversity and individuality are the point.<br /> <br /> You might argue that you can defend your use of &quot;body horror&quot; in the same way, but I would disagree. However, it depends on a bit of clarification: when you say &quot;body<b> horror,</b>&quot; are you treating that as synonymous with &quot;body <b>modification</b>&quot;? I would treat those as distinct, but not entirely unrelated, concepts.<br /> <br /> For example, a Metamorphosist who uses Vicissitude to move their heart to a different part of their body as a defence against being staked is definitely engaging in body modification. But while it might be disgusting to watch, I don't think most folks would consider what amounts to a surgical procedure to be a form of body horror.<br /> <br /> For more of a grey area, if the Metamorphosist instead opted to strengthen their ribcage by reinforcing it with other rib bones (using the 6-dot power that lets you graft on other peoples' body parts), then that would probably count as body horror from the perspective of the person who probably has to be kept alive while their ribs are pulled out and moulded onto the Tzimisce's chest, while still also being body modification. And the appearance of the Tzimisce after the process may not be particularly &quot;horrifying.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, of course, a Tzimisce who turns themself into a writhing-mass of lamprey-like tentacles has probably crossed over properly into something you could call body horror.<br /> <br /> Now, usual caveats around personal taste, do what you want at your table, etc., part of why I'm pushing back against your Stereotype of Metamorphosis-as-body-horror is because, in my opinion, that is the Absolute Worst element of the Path of Metamorphosis and how it has sometimes been portrayed. Again, not because it's &quot;gross.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's because it's stupid.<br /> <br /> The idea of Tzimisce/Metamorphosists going out of their way to make themselves look monstrous as some kind of rejection of their humanity is childish edge-lord nonsense. They're still letting themselves be defined by humanity through their opposition to it. At best, it makes sense as a silly phase that Tzimisce neonates go through before they &quot;grow up&quot; and get serious about Metamorphosis. A better example of what a &quot;mature&quot; Metamorphosist might sound like would be Alucard telling Walter &quot;the trappings of mortal form are meaningless to me.&quot; Another good example is how Yorak's &quot;default&quot; appearance was that of an old man, despite Yorak being basically the Paragon of Metamorphosis in their night.<br /> <br /> A mature Metamorphosist would not let themselves get hung up on &quot;looking like a monster.&quot; They would coldly and rationally consider what form will best enable them to pursue their own ideal form of vampirism. A Metamorphosist who makes themself look monstrous because they think making their prey afraid will help them hunt is just as valid as a Metamorphosist who makes themself look as blandly human as possible as a form of camouflage for the hunt. What matters is that they are motivated by their desire to become a Perfect Being, not by their desire to give the concept of humanity the middle finger.<br /> <br /> In the words of Hannibal Lecter, &quot;No, [body horror] is coincidental!&quot;<br /> <br /> And, again, while taste and such are subjective, there are clear signs that some of the writers have come around to this way of thinking. Even by the time of Revised, you had various factions and ideologies among the Tzimisce that rejected the &quot;body horror&quot; concept, with groups like the Old Clan and the Children of the Dracon. But it's even more prominent in V20, with the Tzimisce write-up in (IIRC) <u>Lore of the Clans</u> basically being a discussion of how the obsession with monstrosity could be a sign of Kupala's corrupting influence. You can see a similar attitude in the discussion between Beckett and Vykos in BJD regarding the latter's decision to mutilate themself just to make a rhetorical point. Entertainingly edgy, sure, but still childish and stupid, for reasons that can easily be spelled out (pun intended).<br /> <br /> Again, if you can manage to sum all that up into a tidy little Stereotype you can easily share with someone, great. But I'm not shedding any tears if you can't. And I (playfully) think it's downright disrespectful to try and force the Path of Metamorphosis into the Worst Possible Stereotype you can imagine for it.<br /> <br /> (P.S. I've talked a lot about Stereotypes, and that term tends to be treated as inherently negative or pejorative. To be clear, I'm trying to use it in a neutral manner here, just as a description of what you seem to be talking about. Stereotypes are a kind of heuristic, and heuristics are useful. But they have limits, and you need to be careful of them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna go with the monstrous transhumanist body horror stuff cause that's what's fun about the path and what's in the book description.<br /> I never said body horror is gross I said it's easy to explain to a player they don't have to lean into that. I gave an example of doing so <i>&quot;Oh you don't have to do that if you think it's gross&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Oh yeah on topic sin 6 and 3 feels off, 6 sort of encourages arguing with your party and sin 3 feels like it'd trigger pretty often for being so low. Other than that I think it looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","user":"Tjalei","date":". 09-01-2026, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T00:30:47-07:00","id":1563744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563717#post1563717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because it's stupid.<br /> <br /> The idea of Tzimisce/Metamorphosists going out of their way to make themselves look monstrous as some kind of rejection of their humanity is childish edge-lord nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about edginess, it's about spiting God!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T00:54:24-07:00","id":1563745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563742#post1563742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna go with the monstrous transhumanist body horror stuff cause that's what's fun about the path and what's in the book description.<br /> I never said body horror is gross I said it's easy to explain to a player they don't have to lean into that. I gave an example of doing so <i>&quot;Oh you don't have to do that if you think it's gross&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that <b>you</b> think body horror is gross. But you <b>were</b> the one who brought it up first. I just responded, and I feel like the &quot;gross&quot; part made up a pretty small part of my response. The majority of my commentary was on the problem of trying to reduce the Path to a Stereotype, and I don't see an actual response to the main thrust of my argument in any of what you just said.<br /> <br /> Like I said, your taste is your taste, and your table is your table. But it kind of sounds like the start and finish of your understanding of the Path is based on the write-up in the Core rules, maybe with some extra bits from the wiki. And those of us who have read a little more may not take that seriously, and will say as much when you start asserting that a different Path is invalid because you can't boil it down to a Stereotype, and use your narrow viewpoint on the Path of Metamorphosis as a justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T00:57:19-07:00","id":1563746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563744#post1563744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about edginess, it's about spiting God!</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:red\">[Citation needed]</span></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  Let's lean into that Hbomb reference 09-01-2026, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T01:12:09-07:00","id":1563747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563746#post1563746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Citation needed]</div> </div> </div> </div>The citation is myself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T01:22:24-07:00","id":1563748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563747#post1563747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The citation is myself!</div> </div> </div> </div>Plot Twist!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T03:46:13-07:00","id":1563750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563742#post1563742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna go with the monstrous transhumanist body horror stuff cause that's what's fun about the path and what's in the book description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go with whatever you want, but saying the Path is X because you like X is objectively an error, not a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> Metamorphosis is designed to be broader and does not follow your view of &quot;clearly defined role&quot;. Period. It giving you an easy stereotype to lean on if you don't want to engage with its open nature doesn't change that it is not what you claimed it to be.<br /> <br /> It's also not exactly what's in the description, as the description makes a point to say this is not the only approach, in fact not even common among older practitioners. You're making a selective reading, which is more about you and what you like in the Path than about the Path.<br /> <br /> And that's what's fun for you. The Path isn't an open framework just for the sake of being, it is also because plenty of people have different opinions on what's a fun approach to its key concepts and what is boring. I personally find the body horror stupidly boring, yet I do like the Transhumanist idea and several of the other things that can be done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T04:40:26-07:00","id":1563755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563719#post1563719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;27477&quot;]While the seeking self-knowledge part is important, having &quot;Self-deception&quot; as the Rank 1 Sin may make it a bit easier to qualify what counts as a transgression. &quot;The True Will must Know Itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> The act of pursuing self-knowledge may work better at Rank 2, analogous to &quot;Neglecting to alter one's body&quot; on the Path of Metamorphosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-deception will be explicit in the Rationale, but I need this one to be broader so I can fill it with meaning in the description. If I want to include the process of revision of the Self, I can't make it too narrow. I like the phrasing in this case because it makes it obvious there is a &quot;how do I do that&quot;.<br /> It's also a Rank 1 Sin in Eightfold Wheel, although woefully unclear unless you bring knowledge of how the philosophy behind the faith it is based on to the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563719#post1563719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it needs to be defined more, I think it might be a good idea to replace &quot;self-interest&quot; with &quot;True Will&quot; in the Rank 4 Sin, just because of the common connotations of &quot;self-interest&quot; maybe obscuring the intended meaning a bit. While I understand it's inclusion better, I worry that &quot;Treat others as you wish to be treated&quot; might similarly carry too much conceptual baggage. Even if they stay as placeholders, those particular concepts could maybe be rephrased to connect them better with the elaboration you'll eventually be providing on the deeper philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to avoid bringing True Will back into the concrete Sins as much as possible. Let's be real, the first thing a player looks at after reading the name of the Path is the Hierarchy. The start of the thread makes it pretty obvious how off-putting that can be without context, and as was rightly pointed out it also makes application of the Sins a lot less intuitive.<br /> Same goes for &quot;Treat others as you wish to be treated&quot;; while it may not transport the specific application, it works very well for transporting the general idea. That is enough if I can contextualize it later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563719#post1563719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I had for a &quot;custom&quot; Sin that might be appropriate to the Path is &quot;Thoughtless destruction.&quot; It leaves a lot of room for calculated violence, but condemns reckless and impulsive aggression, along with excessive collateral damage. I'd probably slot that into the Rank 4-6 range somewhere, but it's just an idea for you to consider. Similarly, &quot;Acting on impulse&quot; could work well as an option for the higher Ranks, could replace the altered Frenzy Sin, especially if you consider Frenzy as an &quot;impulse,&quot; but I think it may also cover the short-vs-long-term stuff you have at Rank 7 a bit more succinctly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I considered something like &quot;Thoughtless destruction&quot;, but decided against it since the other Sins make it a bit obsolete. There is enough incentive already to disencourage impulsive or thoughtless action, I think. Also, if you go back to my first post and read the Sins, it's all there - I don't want to fall into circles.<br /> That said, your suggestions make perfect sense. I just think I need to draw a line somewhere and rely on my previous decisions or I will fiddle with this forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563719#post1563719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like &quot;Yielding personal freedom,&quot; it does a good job of covering a lot of ground while still being well-defined and consistent with the spirit of the Path. And Rank 3 is a nice and dramatically-appropriate place to put it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563742#post1563742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah on topic sin 6 and 3 feels off, 6 sort of encourages arguing with your party and sin 3 feels like it'd trigger pretty often for being so low. Other than that I think it looks good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Rank 3 is a good spot, but I will change &quot;Yielding&quot; to &quot;Forfeiting&quot;, that should exclude temporary transgressions (like, being Dominated).<br /> If I touch up Rank 6 to something like &quot;Thoughtless action&quot; I would need to increase the Rank; I think the spot it currently has is good for the scope. Social friction was the point, after all - and as an aside, I have yet to play with a group where constant bickering over minutiae isn't a feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T08:32:30-07:00","id":1563771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563478-feedback-on-a-homebrew-path-of-enlightenment-v20?p=1563755#post1563755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-deception will be explicit in the Rationale, but I need this one to be broader so I can fill it with meaning in the description. If I want to include the process of revision of the Self, I can't make it too narrow. I like the phrasing in this case because it makes it obvious there is a &quot;how do I do that&quot;.<br /> It's also a Rank 1 Sin in Eightfold Wheel, although woefully unclear unless you bring knowledge of how the philosophy behind the faith it is based on to the table.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to avoid bringing True Will back into the concrete Sins as much as possible. Let's be real, the first thing a player looks at after reading the name of the Path is the Hierarchy. The start of the thread makes it pretty obvious how off-putting that can be without context, and as was rightly pointed out it also makes application of the Sins a lot less intuitive.<br /> Same goes for &quot;Treat others as you wish to be treated&quot;; while it may not transport the specific application, it works very well for transporting the general idea. That is enough if I can contextualize it later.<br /> <br /> <br /> I considered something like &quot;Thoughtless destruction&quot;, but decided against it since the other Sins make it a bit obsolete. There is enough incentive already to disencourage impulsive or thoughtless action, I think. Also, if you go back to my first post and read the Sins, it's all there - I don't want to fall into circles.<br /> That said, your suggestions make perfect sense. I just think I need to draw a line somewhere and rely on my previous decisions or I will fiddle with this forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are fair points. I definitely agree that most of my suggestions only make sense as alternatives if you're removing other things, so I get it if you prefer the versions you have now.<br /> <br /> But while I get your point that the Hierarchy of Sins is the first thing people are going to look at, I think it's a bit cart-before-the-horse to focus on that too much when so much of the philosophical underpinnings still need to be contextualized, as you put it. At this point, I understand that I'm missing a lot of the background information that helps make sense of the Path and its Hierarchy of Sins, but that kind of means that I can't really speak to whether the Hierarchy of Sins you've constructed works or not, because I'm missing so much of the context that should be attached to the Sins you've chosen. And I would be wary of borrowing the wording from different Hierarchies without considering that they only make sense within their specific context.<br /> <br /> So I guess I'm saying that now is probably a good time to shift focus and work on fleshing those parts out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T09:43:25-07:00","id":1563772,"title":"","content":"Working on it. And while fixing the Hierarchy first seems like a reversal of procedure, for me it's more like making a recipe. I have a list I can work along now, and can add spices later if needed.<br /> <br /> This may take a while, though. I have some RL stuff to attend and it's probably going to be weekend-only thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T06:52:18-07:00","id":1563853,"title":"","content":"Current revision.<br /> <br /> I added some fluff - hopefully not too purple - to use as some help with reconstruct the Path development and the reasoning behind it at the same time. Making True Will the goal and method at the same time was a priority. I tried to use the discussions in this thread as a guide and incorporate it as a means to answer potential questions, although being that far involved makes a neutral point of view very difficult. I added a bit of practice to make things easier to follow.<br /> <br /> Also while editing, I noticed some trace amounts of Stirner and Rand that I had to tweak, but I think they add some spice to it. The ethics were expanded to include some of the more practical elements on how to resolve apparent conflicts between them.<br /> <br /> If you think parts of the description don't fit or are missing, let me know. Mostly I'm interested in whether the concept is understandable now, though.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Path of Desire and True Will (V3)</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>As I travel through the night, the sun shines only on the road behind me; </i><br /> <i>but I know these steps by heart, and my will lights the way. </i><br /> <br /> <i>A hungry beast stalks me, to scavenge on my spoils or corpse; </i><br /> <i>but shared meals and victories have tamed it, and now my will guides its strikes.</i><br /> <br /> <i>When I meet you on the path we shall journey together: </i><br /> <i>for gods above and below are silent when they find themselves in obsolescence.</i><br /> <br /> - Three Books Without Name, Book I, Chapter I</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Travelers on this Path need to find their True Will, a harmonious integration of their desires and self-realization with their Beast and society. Because True Will also includes the journey to find itself, it is an ideal that is aspired to but never attained.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The main source for the philosophy of the Path is the first of the <i>Three B</i><i>ook</i><i>s</i><i> Without Name</i>. The oldest extant copy (as <i>Sine Nomine Libris Tres</i>) is safely locked away in the collection of a Sabbat scholar, but modern translated versions keep finding their way into the hands of young seekers. There are no known extant copies of the remaining two volumes, if they ever existed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Very few details can be glimpsed about the anonymous author as they write from the point of view of an abstract persona, but the scholars who have bothered to examine this curiosity in detail speculate its origin lies somewhere in the Maghrib of the Renaissance. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A single reference to a third eye invites speculation they could be a Childe of Saulot, but this is pure conjecture on what is more likely just a simple metaphor. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">At some point, the author had access to <i>On Hunger and its Satisfaction</i> by the Brujah philosopher Tanitbaal-Sahar as evidenced by verbatim quotes. They likely have traveled on the Road of Sin, but must have fallen from it at some point. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Isolated and in danger of Wassail, they undertook a spiritual journey and rebuilt themselves from their lowest point: as the book tells it, the Path of Desire and True Will was developed while the author traveled on it, in the same process of refinement that the Path itself describes as one of its most important epiphanies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Reduced to a shell, a Wight is a dead body with a Beast. The spark that differentiates Cainite from Wight is desire: the desire to be more than a Beast, the desire to <i>be </i>and<i> become</i>. The author postulates that since the desire to exist in a void would be pointless, one must understand the world, their place in it and what reality one wants to live in. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">These realizations are not trivial - each carries consequences in how they influence ones actions, and these actions in turn have consequences that change the world one tries to place themselves into. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The result is a causal loop that requires steady re-examination of whether that understanding still holds true, or in a word, to find self-knowledge. On this basis, one is then able to build the second central concept of the Path: finding True Will.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">This concept is again ostensibly shared with the Road of Sin, but despite the name it is almost the complete opposite. Will based solely on the self or base desires is too limited and ignorant, it is only self-deception. Neither is True Will a measure of direct satisfaction, it is commitment to a goal built while being mindful of the consequences, because an unwanted consequence is a direct failure of self-knowledge. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A goal that ignores the world - or more immediate, community - is not serving True Will because it would ignore the desire to care by ones own nature and is a part of it as a fact of reality. True Will must fit the world, and the world must fit True Will: if ones actions make society reject them, or degrade it into a society they would not want to live in, they were not actions of Will, but of ignorance.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Path is highly skeptical of ritualized actions, as these tend to mindlessly repeat instructions without verifying whether the underlying reason for them still holds true. The only ritual found in the Books Without Name is consequently called the Breaking Ritual. Its purpose is to verify whether the practitioner's True Will is, indeed, still their True Will and to prevent it from becoming itself ritual. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">As everything about the Path is highly individualistic, there is no formal way of performing it. Some use divination as an aid, others meditation. Some talk to their reflection in a mirror, very few discuss it with confidants. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The goal is however the same: stripping down what they are to the core, and rebuild themselves following each step they took on their way to the True Will, examining every part for its validity. Encountering a mismatch means they will have to mend that damage, and adjust it to fit with their current True Will. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Because it is a very taxing and potentially dangerous process to their Self, the Breaking Ritual is usually only performed when a traveler on the Path encounters a roadblock they can not circumnavigate by other means.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">In practice, a new initiate on the Path will perform their first Breaking Ritual under guidance, either by a fellow traveler or the detailed instructions in the book. Formulating the first iteration of their True Will, they need a clear vision of what their future should and will look like, and see a path towards their goal. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once their True Will has been established, it becomes the only authority they will follow, and any other authority must match or at least not contradict its paradigm. Storytellers and players should use this opportunity to discuss the character's concept, how their True Will would dictate their actions, and what conflicts with it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Virtues:</b> Conscience, Self-Control</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ethics:</b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Act mindful. All your actions will be reflected back onto you.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Beast belongs to you, but you do not belong to it.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Harmony is not conformity. Two voices with different tones can be harmonic.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Do not compromise, but share in mutual desires.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Freedom, control, and will are your most valuable tools. Do not lose them.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Beware hidden authority. It lurks behind all rituals and concepts.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Destiny is never dictated, but found through self-knowledge.</span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Hierarchy of Sins</b></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Path of Desire and True Will</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rating</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Moral Guideline</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rationale</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">10</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Feeling guilt for your actions</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There can be no guilt in mindful action</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">9</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failing to explore a new desire</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Desire is kindling, do not let it run out</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">8</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Refusing indulgence that harms none</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Desire needs to burn to placate the Beast</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">7</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Forfeiting long-term for short-term progress</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There are no shortcuts to your destiny</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">6</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Putting desires of Beast or man before yours</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">No-one but yourself must control you</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure to treat others as you would be treated</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There can be no harmony in imbalance</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Acting against your own self interests</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Always evaluate, but never compromise</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Forfeiting a personal freedom</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Your freedom is your greatest tool</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Losing Will or Virtue</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Your will is your strongest resource</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure to seek self-knowledge</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Self-deception obscures the Path ahead </span></td> </tr> </table></div> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}